	file.0000000000000001.title: "&l&6Society: Sunlit Valley"
	quest.001F144802D59DB4.quest_desc: ["The &6Ender Hook&r is the fastest and highest range of all hooks, but only has one hook. Best for traveling, not as good for building."]
	quest.003782D1F1A74349.quest_desc: [
		"&6Growth Obelisks&r are a farmer's best friend, harnessing Ribbit magic to grow crops in a wide area around them every morning at 7am."
		""
		"Every time they work, they consume 1 &6Spark-Gro&r, a delicate mix of fertilizers and &6Sparkstone&r."
	]
	quest.003782D1F1A74349.quest_subtitle: "It's what plants crave"
	quest.018699F88064119B.quest_desc: ["The most important alloy for progression is &6Brass&r. It is a combination of Copper and Zinc, with Iridium Scrap used as a catalyst."]
	quest.01B84BE72772B00B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lead&r is a secondary material needed for heavy machinery."
		""
		"It can be found in the &6Skull Cavern&r, increasing in frequency the deeper you go."
	]
	quest.01B84BE72772B00B.title: "Cavern Metal I"
	quest.022DC375C4F2360A.quest_subtitle: "Nether Structures"
	quest.0327B9F8868AE76E.quest_desc: [
		"Once the Community Center is complete, excluding the Abandoned Farm, the &6Witch&r villager will sell you a &6Ribbit Hut&r!"
		""
		"This building houses Ribbits that can use their powerful magic to harvest crops in a large area around it without any upkeep!"
		""
		"This is a large building, requiring a 3x3x3 area of space to place. You can access its inventory from the door block."
	]
	quest.0327B9F8868AE76E.title: "Ribbit Harvesting"
	quest.03773C88CA88552A.quest_desc: ["&6Geode Nodes&r rarely found in caves have a chance of dropping &6Aquamarine,&r the main crafting material for fishing related tools. "]
	quest.038D4A6A3CA1C015.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Pickling Can&r is an efficient way to pickle certain vegetables."
		""
		"It requires adjacent Salt Layers produced by an &6Evaporator&r, but does its job faster than other methods. "
		""
		"High quality vegetables will produce high quality pickles!"
	]
	quest.038D4A6A3CA1C015.title: "Quality Pickling"
	quest.03F3D0F74A5BC0C4.title: "Freshwater Fish Bundle"
	quest.0403045A4DA7A770.title: "Artisan's Bundle"
	quest.0462313FFAEC4054.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Electricity Generator&r is capable of burning coal to power certain furniture devices."
		""
		"Most importantly, it poweres the &6Workbench&r, which can craft various furniture blocks that are otherwise difficult to obtain."
		""
		"You can link generators to blocks that need power using the &6Electric Wrench&r."
	]
	quest.0462313FFAEC4054.quest_subtitle: "FE - Furniture Energy"
	quest.0462313FFAEC4054.title: "Furniture Constructing"
	quest.048655663A5A82FC.quest_desc: ["The &6Market&r is the most essential supplier of your farm. It stocks seeds, farming, and cooking supplies."]
	quest.057A1891E5864EBF.quest_desc: [
		"Buying seeds for crops that require them really eats into your margins. The &6Seed Maker&r turns crops into seeds for free."
		""
		"Using crops with any quality will turn the seed into the lowest quality inputed into the &6Seed Maker&r in &61&r day. "
		""
		"Quality seeds will have a higher chance to grow quality crops, making it worth your time to produce good seeds!"
	]
	quest.062C9E95DF7C987D.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		"        Meow?"
	]
	quest.06308BDE5F4EC0D2.quest_desc: [
		"Normally farm animals are picky about their living conditions and food! The &6Witch&r sells ancient magic that can shrink them into a plushie, making it a luxurious home."
		""
		"Plushies that have been imbued using a &6Sunlit Crystal&r will have special effects "
		""
		"&oBoth the plushie and the animal must be at max affection.&r"
	]
	quest.065A8A3BFFA00CB7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Arms&r are a method for transporting items to multiple inputs and outputs. It's handy for automating specific tasks!"
		""
		"You can see a list of valid targets for it on the left side of the ponder menu."
	]
	quest.065A8A3BFFA00CB7.title: "Mechanical Movement"
	quest.06EDF98282351F85.title: "Complete the Vault"
	quest.071B9936A0F6425F.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.071B9936A0F6425F.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.07858B887B222BC2.quest_desc: [
		"While caving, you might come across these rare minerals."
		""
		"&6Earth Crystals&r are an important crafting ingredient, so collect as many as you can."
		""
		"Their soft glow gives them away in dark caves."
	]
	quest.07858B887B222BC2.title: "Hidden in the Stone"
	quest.07938A28F31B7473.quest_desc: ["&6Plant Nutrients&r are made from Weak Fertilizer and can be used for crafting more advanced versions of them."]
	quest.07938A28F31B7473.quest_subtitle: "Its got electrolytes"
	quest.07A551F04BB9A117.quest_desc: [
		"Slimes' happiness depends on their hunger and living conditions. Every time they eat, their &6happiness&r will increase. If they're surrounded by similar types of Slimes, they'll get happier!"
		""
		"Happiness decreases when Slimes are hungry or crowded (more than &67&r in an area)."
		""
		"When unhappy, Slimes may cause status effects to their surroundings. The more valuable their Plorts are, the more deadly they may be..."
	]
	quest.07A551F04BB9A117.title: "Slime Happiness"
	quest.07D5EB5853F9A357.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Template Manager&r allows you to create and upload schematics! These can be used in other worlds, making it a good way to design buildings in creative and auto-build them in survival."
		""
		"A &6Copy-Paste&r gadget is needed for this to be useful."
	]
	quest.07D5EB5853F9A357.title: "Schematics!"
	quest.08241E18191275AE.title: "Iron Tools"
	quest.086A3F527E1A973E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Angel Core&r lets you to place blocks in midair using wands."
		""
		"The &6Destruction Core&r allows you to void blocks the same way that you build them with a wand."
	]
	quest.086A3F527E1A973E.title: "Building Wand Cores"
	quest.08CFE766C9645FC8.quest_desc: [
		"High quality items can lead to a huge increase in profits, but it can make automation and storage a hassle."
		""
		"The &6Quality Washer&r removes quality from crops inserted into it, pushing it into the inventory below."
	]
	quest.08CFE766C9645FC8.title: "Removing Quality"
	quest.094497558E9DB19C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Advanced Wine Kegs&r need juice, empty wine bottles, and their ingredients to work. The juice a given wine needs can be found in the recipe using JEI by hovering over the bar in the middle."
		""
		"Recipes can use the following juices:"
		""
		"- &cRed&r/&aWhite&r grape juice"
		"- &cCrimson&r/&aWarped&r grape juice"
		"- &eApple Juice&r (made using an Apple Press)"
		""
		"Juices are inserted in the top left slot of the Fermentation Barrel."
	]
	quest.094497558E9DB19C.title: "Juicing up the Wine"
	quest.09ADAEA86CEB55E2.title: "Master Brewer"
	quest.0A1FA99B227284C7.quest_desc: [
		"Clocking in at &616 million &rcoins, the &6Golden Clock&r is one of the most excruciatingly and unnecessarily expensive items in the game."
		""
		"It will randomly progress all artisan machines in its 5x5x5 area, centered around the clock."
		""
		"Not that you really need the money at this point."
	]
	quest.0A1FA99B227284C7.quest_subtitle: "The Money Sink"
	quest.0A1FA99B227284C7.title: "The Golden Clock"
	quest.0A39B0C0A77E57B0.quest_desc: [
		"Once you find an appropriate place to start your farm, your first step should be preparing a field of farmland."
		""
		"Once your crops are fully grown, you can &6Right Click&r to harvest without losing the seed! Hoes can do this an an area."
	]
	quest.0A39B0C0A77E57B0.title: "Preparing the Fields"
	quest.0A455A4E0D7D074E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Greenhouse Glass&r is a special material that lets crops up to 16 blocks underneath grow during any season."
		""
		"It's probably far too expensive at this point in the game to craft, but a few blocks over key crops can make a difference."
	]
	quest.0AC36BAB58CFD71D.quest_subtitle: "Killing Creepers"
	quest.0ACB2E342421B74E.title: "Iron Armor"
	quest.0B0AC1BFF726E11E.title: "Butterfly \\& Moth Collection Complete!"
	quest.0B45A918213371FA.quest_desc: ["Only &63&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.0B45A918213371FA.title: "Mineralogist's Bundle"
	quest.0B85DF081F75ECA7.quest_desc: ["The &dGalaxy Sword&r is one of the most powerful swords in the game. It can be crafted with a &dPrismatic Shard&r and an Iridium Sword.."]
	quest.0BE5F31F09A945C1.title: "Master Barista"
	quest.0C17CF9D782787BE.title: "Fish Collection Complete!"
	quest.0C5B1C74E340882B.quest_desc: [
		"Minecarts are an early-mid game form of transport for both items, players, and mobs."
		""
		"They are simple but elegant, and have options to make them even faster."
	]
	quest.0C5EB5F66FB04A29.quest_desc: [
		"Not all mushrooms can be cultivated on &6Mushroom Soil&r. The power of the &6Mossberry&r can be used to make the &6Mushroom Log&r!"
		""
		"It draws from nearby trees to form different kinds of mushrooms every 4 days depending on the tree types. "
		""
		"The quantity and quality of them is impacted by the amount of nearby trees."
	]
	quest.0C7D8F89BCF645AA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Charging Rods&r take lightning from storms and create Batteries, used in crafting items that use electricity."
		""
		"They don't work in Winter, as no stormy weather occurs."
	]
	quest.0C7D8F89BCF645AA.title: "Capturing Lightning"
	quest.0D400BA3A1431963.quest_subtitle: "Nether"
	quest.0DC68C5CF6D82372.quest_desc: [
		"The second layer consists of two different ice biomes: the Frozen Caves and Frozen Maelstrom. By now you may have noticed two things:"
		""
		"- Certain mobs only spawn in certain biomes"
		"- Blocks you place in the Skull Cavern don't get destroyed overnight."
		""
		"Use these facts to your advantage to get lower faster, especially since this layer will start to be a real challenge from mobs..."
	]
	quest.0DC68C5CF6D82372.title: "Layer II - Frozen Depths"
	quest.0E13E56F342F243F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Black Opal&r upgrade can be used on a &6Crystalarium&r to let it produce Pristine versions of the mineral or gem grown."
		""
		"Not only are these more valuable, but they can also be broken down into multiple of the basic versions."
	]
	quest.0E4EA6B5E8E6361C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Jade&r can be found by mining &6Omni Geode Nodes&r scattered around the caverns. The deeper you descend, the more likely you are to encounter them."
		""
		"It is a crucial crafting mineral used in a variety of useful farming machines."
	]
	quest.0E68DD5DFB2DFD97.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit trees slowly grow fruits that can be hand picked. "
		""
		"A handfull of basic ones can be purchased from the Market, but you'll need to dive into the &6Skull Cavern&r for more advanced ones."
		""
		"The fruits can be moved by breaking them with &6Shears&r and placed under other leaves."
	]
	quest.0E68DD5DFB2DFD97.title: "Fruit Trees"
	quest.0E7AAB1F6C287535.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Book Fair&r appears at the end of every season (for example, Late Spring)."
		""
		"Skill books that are normally found in the world can be bought for high prices, with some rotating stock every season."
	]
	quest.0E93089181D8EE7B.quest_desc: ["Minecarts can be linked using the &6Mob Spring&r or &6Cart Coupling&r."]
	quest.0E93089181D8EE7B.title: "Linking Carts"
	quest.0EE5A175B0417403.quest_desc: [
		"&6Watering Cans&r can be upgraded to hold more water, work faster, and also work in an area!"
		""
		"Hold &6Shift + Right Click&r to charge up the area of affect watering ability. Higher tiers have higher areas!"
	]
	quest.0EE5A175B0417403.title: "Upgraded Watering"
	quest.0F176FBF01ABB774.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fire Quartz&r is the gate to more advanced farming equipment."
		""
		"It can be found scattered around the Nether, and glows brightly."
	]
	quest.0F606FEB98D44C0F.quest_desc: ["Only &63&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.0F606FEB98D44C0F.title: "Adventurer's Bundle"
	quest.0F77A3F0506C76B2.quest_desc: ["&6Wooden Rails&r are cheaper, with a slower maximum speed."]
	quest.0F8E0141BDC23F7B.quest_desc: [
		"Holding the &6w&r key while hovering over a Create item will let you see detailed information about it."
		""
		"If something isn't explained in this quest chapter, chances are it's explained with Ponder!"
	]
	quest.0F8E0141BDC23F7B.title: "Hold [&6W&r] to Ponder"
	quest.0FA01C816AE13170.quest_subtitle: "Skull Cavern"
	quest.0FF95378E683DF5E.quest_desc: [
		"Can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.0FF95378E683DF5E.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.100B4D3BEEE9C433.quest_desc: [
		"To craft special furniture using the &6Workbench&r, you may need items purchased from a catalog."
		""
		"These can be bought from a &6Witch&r, and placed in world. "
		""
		"Right click them with &6Coins&r to purchase the crafting items for that furniture set."
	]
	quest.100B4D3BEEE9C433.title: "Furniture Catalogs"
	quest.1030BCF34FEAE03C.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Splendid Slime&r has different effects that may happen when they are unhappy or happy."
		""
		"On top of that, Slimes may also have &6Traits&r: different behaviors or quirks that make ranching them more difficult."
		""
		"Always check the traits of a Slime you're ranching by looking at the uses of a Slime in item form using JEI!"
		""
		"&oRocket Pods can be launched at your feet using the Slime Vac to rocket jump.&r"
	]
	quest.1030BCF34FEAE03C.title: "Slime Traits"
	quest.10C0B87E2EA1C8A5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hooks&r allow you to get out of ditches fast and climb tall mountains."
		""
		"They need to be in your curio slot and are activated using a hotkey."
		""
		"You can buy one from the &6Guild&r."
	]
	quest.10EC025C45540E52.title: "24,576 Bundle"
	quest.11207C347FC407E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eElectrum Tools&r increase in damage the faster the wearer is. This combines well with the armor, allowing you to rip and tear through mobs."
		""
		"They also come built in with &6Fortune III&r."
	]
	quest.11207C347FC407E1.quest_subtitle: "Requires Create or Botania"
	quest.11207C347FC407E1.title: "Electrum Tools"
	quest.115795B60C6CA0ED.quest_desc: [
		"Mining ore in the Skull Cavern has a chance to drop &6Omni Geodes&r."
		""
		"They can be extracted for any tier of mineral, and have a chance to drop &6Iridium Scrap&r and &dPrismatic Shards&r when extracted."
	]
	quest.11A36B05684D70A9.quest_desc: [
		"In the Nether, native fish can be caught using the &6Lava Fishing Rod&r. "
		""
		"They will also randomly upgrade enchantments from succesful catches."
		""
		"Since the Nether has no season, the same fish can be caught at any time. Some fish are biome dependent though."
	]
	quest.122BB9885C33C85F.quest_desc: [
		"Cooking is essential early on, for both keeping you alive in the mines and making profit."
		""
		"A few basic ones can be crafted using &6Earth Crystals&r."
		""
		"In general, cooked meals are worth &61.2x-2x the sum of their ingredients&r! Complex dishes (ones with many ingredients) have an additional boost to their value as well."
	]
	quest.122BB9885C33C85F.title: "Getting Cooking"
	quest.1254F6F99ABB36D5.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.12716A71DB8FB7B8.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.12716A71DB8FB7B8.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.1280C34AE9A4EE7B.quest_desc: ["Cook all dishes from &6Let's Do: Candlelight&r."]
	quest.1280C34AE9A4EE7B.title: "Candlelight Champion"
	quest.12ED0E637AD47FD4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Workbench&r is used for crafting advanced furniture, and blocks from furniture catalogs!"
		""
		"It can be purchased from the &6Blacksmith&r but requires power to operate. "
		""
		"You can burn solid fuel in a generator and connect it to the &6Workbench&r using the &6Electric Wrench&r."
	]
	quest.12ED0E637AD47FD4.title: "Furniture Crafting"
	quest.12FC0701CC742176.quest_desc: [
		"&6Recall Potions&r are consumables found throughout the world or brewed that will take you home from anywhere."
		""
		"Usefull early on for exploring without missing 6am!"
	]
	quest.1301B3E1ABF40A99.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Market&r will stock new crops after one full year of playtime."
		""
		"The &6Starfruit Sapling&r can be obtained with &dPrismatic Shards&r alongside a hefty price."
		""
		"It is the most valuable tree fruit in the game, and can be made into the expensive brew &6Star Coquito&r."
	]
	quest.13298D80ED38BE30.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.1348507AE17E187E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Trader&r offers wares that can only be purchased with items and not money."
		""
		"The Trader can be invited on the phone after visiting the &6Skull Cavern&r for the first time."
	]
	quest.1348507AE17E187E.title: "Trader"
	quest.1375AE2ECAC8C147.quest_desc: [
		"Want to protect your base or keep it loaded? Chunks can be claimed using the JourneyMap - &6j&r key by default."
		""
		"First, click the \"FTBChunks Claming Mode\" button on the right side. Then:"
		"- &6Left-Click&r to claim a chunk"
		"- &6Right-Click&r to remove the claim"
		""
		"- &6Shift&r + &6Left-Clicking&r to forceload a chunk (up to 15)"
		"- &6Shift&r + &6Right-Clicking&r to un-forceload the chunk"
	]
	quest.1375AE2ECAC8C147.title: "Claiming Chunks"
	quest.139B02AFBCBBF350.quest_desc: [
		"During exploration you may have come across a &6Slime Heart&r. These are precious items that can be used to begin Slime Incubating!"
		""
		"To start, right click a &6Slime Incubator&r with the heart."
	]
	quest.139B02AFBCBBF350.title: "Slime Incubating"
	quest.140472B5516ED9F1.quest_desc: [
		"Gold and Silver alloys into &6Electrum&r. This is primarily an ingredient for upgrading tools and armor."
		""
		"The tools do more damage the faster you are, while the armor pieces passively make you faster."
	]
	quest.146475549DD7BF4A.quest_desc: [
		"The final layer of the &6Skull Cavern&r holds two different biomes."
		""
		"One of them is the &6Umbra Barrens&r, a place you might find familiar from another world..."
		""
		"&oIf you haven't noticed there is no End in Sunlit Valley.&r"
	]
	quest.146475549DD7BF4A.title: "The Bottom of the Skull Cavern"
	quest.15061E71D3F55AE8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Refined Storage systems&r aren't great at handling many different types of non-stacking items!"
		""
		"Avoid dumping all your plushies in your system, and store them in large chests instead."
		""
		"This is especially important in multiplayer servers!"
	]
	quest.15061E71D3F55AE8.title: "Avoiding Refined Lag"
	quest.1571D0424A7A34D1.quest_desc: ["&6Butterfly Feeders&r can be placed and filled with Sugar Water to strength butterflies as well as make them more trusting of nearby players."]
	quest.162C1DFB58132D45.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Printer&r can be used to duplicate enchanted books with liquid experience."
		""
		"This can be harvested from items or players using a &6Disenchanter&r."
		""
		"&6Liquid Hyper Experience&r can be used to increase the level of the enchanted book by I, even past normal limits."
	]
	quest.162C1DFB58132D45.title: "Copying Enchanted Books"
	quest.164AAAAD6433695A.quest_desc: [
		"The End does not exist in Sunlit Valley."
		""
		"To craft an &6Elytra&r, you'll need to purchase the expensive parts, and conquer the &6Skull Cavern&r."
		""
		"Alternatively, an &6Abandoned Farm&r may be repaired to obtain one..."
	]
	quest.164AAAAD6433695A.title: "Flying High"
	quest.166D3A381C5C9A8F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Preserve Jars&r turn fruits and vegetables into preserves in &64&r days, multiplying their selling value by over &63&r."
		""
		"Having many run in the background is worth the investment."
	]
	quest.17064AEF4212B5FF.quest_desc: [
		"You've done absolutely everything there is to offer in &6Society: Sunlit Valley&r. Your farm is the envy of all your neighbors for miles."
		""
		"You feel empty inside. The &dTrophy of Perfection&r gives you unlimited &dPrismatic Shards&r, but you fail to see the use of them at this point."
		""
		"...maybe try a speedrun?"
	]
	quest.17064AEF4212B5FF.quest_subtitle: "Realist Capitalist"
	quest.17064AEF4212B5FF.title: "&dPerfection"
	quest.174A6EE7CF7900F0.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Cooking Guide&r allows machines to easily automate the Cooking Pot. "
		""
		"They aren't cheap, but the right farming setup can significantly boost your profits with passive income."
	]
	quest.174A6EE7CF7900F0.title: "Automated Kitchen"
	quest.174FBAB7BF83C049.quest_desc: ["Only &65&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.174FBAB7BF83C049.title: "Foraging Bundle"
	quest.17C8B0197B8636E7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Caterpillar Eggs&r need a safe place to hatch and metamorphosize!"
		""
		"The &6Caterpillar Box&r handles this all for you! Any eggs that are placed inside will eventually turn into beautiful Butterflies and Moths, flying out of the top block."
		""
		"Some types of Butterflies can be difficult to obtain due to how rare they are. Careful breeding can be used to complete your collection or for income!"
	]
	quest.17C8B0197B8636E7.quest_subtitle: "Hobbling towards metamorphosis"
	quest.17D1D7EDA66A95F4.title: "Collection: Minerals"
	quest.17D2933C4B133AA8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Drills&r are simple block breakers whos speed depends on the rotation speed provided. They can be used to build large drills to clear land, or for smaller utility automations."
		""
		"Once crafted, they can be duplicated using a cheaper recipe."
	]
	quest.181794D54A635F81.quest_desc: ["The &6Guild&r will now sell you &6Collar Tags&r, a conduit for enchanting your pets to make them battle-ready."]
	quest.181794D54A635F81.title: "Powerful Beasts"
	quest.1817B00DD389CAE3.quest_subtitle: "Optional"
	quest.18274B43429F2808.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Red Hook&r is a special one that allows you to have creative flight in a small area defined by the hooks."
		""
		"This makes your hook fairly useless for traveling however."
		""
		"Creative flight is rare, so this will likely be your first way of obtaining it."
	]
	quest.18274B43429F2808.quest_subtitle: "Creative-ish flight"
	quest.18490F31FFAB134E.quest_desc: [
		"If you're running a server with more than a handful of people that will be on at seperate times, you should change the season length in the configs."
		""
		"This can be done by changing the &6sub_season_duration&r in &6config/sereneseasons/seasons.toml&r."
		""
		"Having this value set to 16-20 is recommended on larger severs to prevent someone from grinding out an entire season in one day."
	]
	quest.18490F31FFAB134E.title: "For Server Owners"
	quest.187FBE0E4FB5B7AD.quest_desc: [
		"Any compostable material can be used on a &6Worm Farm&r to produce worms."
		""
		"A much cheaper alternative to purchasing them."
	]
	quest.18E4EF841B0D1DC7.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.18E4EF841B0D1DC7.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.19D2D00AC36C9049.title: "Brews Collection Complete!"
	quest.1A1129507F643085.quest_desc: ["Another important use for &6Silver&r is &6Electron Tubes&r. These small lights help provide signaling logic for smarter devices such as &6Brass Funnels&r."]
	quest.1A300B5030B2A1C1.quest_desc: [
		"Turning Eggs into Mayonnaise is a good way of increasing profits from chickens."
		""
		"This can be done with a &6Mayonnaise Machine&r in &61&r day."
		""
		"&oYou'll want to take a look at the farming quest line for information on how to get the ingredients for one.&r"
	]
	quest.1A4FD076999BF29F.quest_desc: [
		"Gather logs and stone, and submit them to this quest in order to receive a free starter farmhouse."
		""
		"You can see a preview of these by talking to Ace the Carpenter and selecting 'Build Farm Buildings'."
	]
	quest.1A4FD076999BF29F.title: "Constructing a Farmhouse"
	quest.1A81A877A381DB97.quest_desc: [
		"Getting to the bottom of the &6Skull Cavern&r can be a challenge. &6Magic Rope&r can be obtained from the Trader to instantly teleport you to the next layer down. "
		""
		"It can also be crafted into a &6Magic Tunnel&r, which teleports you to adjacent caves."
	]
	quest.1A81A877A381DB97.title: "Descending Faster"
	quest.1AA78CF8A14DEE76.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Basic Shipping Bin&r is too simple for mass selling goods as your farm grows."
		""
		"The &6Smart Shipping Bin&r fixes many issues with not being able to sell goods, such as when there's not enough space for coins. It sells every 5 minutes."
		""
		"It will deposit coins directly into your bank account when sold. If you don't have one or its at the limit, it will shoot them out."
		""
		"A &6Basket&r can be placed underneath the output face to capture coins."
	]
	quest.1AA78CF8A14DEE76.title: "Smarter Selling"
	quest.1AADE5D96B701A97.quest_desc: [
		"Brewing beer is a good way to start on producing &6Artisan Goods&r on your farm."
		""
		"Dried ingredients need to be processed in the &6Silo&r."
		""
		"The Brewing process itself requires attention and is slightly complex. You can hold &6W&r while hovering over the Brewingstation to learn how to brew beer."
	]
	quest.1AADE5D96B701A97.title: "Brewing Beer"
	quest.1B614E9E38B45BD0.title: "Wood Tools"
	quest.1B75D6174593D5E5.title: "Geode Mineral Collection Complete!"
	quest.1BA73EA72B471270.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Iridium&r variants of the Backtank and Diving Helmet let you dive in lava, provided you have air."
		""
		"You'll also need the full set of &6Iridium&r equipment to do so."
	]
	quest.1BA73EA72B471270.quest_subtitle: "Lava diving"
	quest.1CA5AF97F26ABC00.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Galaxy Sword&r is an upgrade to an &6Iridium Sword&r that can be made with the &dPrismatic Shard&r."
		""
		"Few weapons rival it in raw power and speed."
	]
	quest.1D21615AEE411491.quest_desc: ["More effective fertilizers can be crafted using &6Plant Nutrients&r. Any good farmer will work towards stockpiling them."]
	quest.1D21615AEE411491.title: "Advanced Fertilizers"
	quest.1D39A308673157BA.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.1D39A308673157BA.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.1D5820FBDD8EB900.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fertilizer&r is a huge step in upgrading how much your farm produces."
		""
		"Simply right click on the farmland to gain the affects. "
	]
	quest.1D5820FBDD8EB900.title: "All on Fertilizers"
	quest.1DC8E69A916864DC.quest_desc: [
		"The next place to exploit for its resources is the &6Nether&r."
		""
		"It's a dangerous place, but has the important resource &6Fire Quartz&r, needed for advanced farm building."
	]
	quest.1DC8E69A916864DC.title: "Getting to the Nether"
	quest.1DCBAC91CE9AAD60.quest_desc: [
		"If you've more than a handful of &6Fish Ponds&r, you may be overflowing with &6Roe&r from fish whos produce items are more valuable than the money its worth."
		""
		"The &6Roe Recycler&r addresses this, allowing you to get a few more chances at items with every peice of roe. "
		""
		"It rolls the entire Fish Pond loot table at a random population for each Roe processed. If it doesn't drop anything, it'll have a 10%% chance to produce &6Algae&r."
	]
	quest.1E2D2FF9428F96DA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Sewing Table&r can cut Artisan Canvas into clothing and hats when combined with other materials."
		""
		"It requires a &6Sewing Needle&r to craft."
		""
		"Crafting it with a &6Chest&r allows it to retain its inventory."
	]
	quest.1E2D2FF9428F96DA.title: "Sewing Clothing"
	quest.1E5531421815CDB3.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrading your tools past wood requires a &6Smithing Table&r. At higher tiers it will require a Smithing Template purchased from a &6Blacksmith Villager&r."
		""
		"Tools can be repaired in an anvil infinitely, and enchantments also carry over when upgrading!"
		""
		"Search for an item in the item list sidebar and &6Left Click&r on it to see its recipes."
	]
	quest.1E5531421815CDB3.title: "Upgrading Tools?"
	quest.1E6139BDE9202B6A.quest_desc: ["Only &66&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.1E6139BDE9202B6A.title: "Chef's Bundle"
	quest.1F0231C09608265D.quest_desc: [
		"You can share a bank account with your friends in multiplayer!"
		""
		"Purchase a &6Blaze Banker&r and a &6White ID Card&r + &6White Card&r for each player from the &6Banker&r villager. Each player must right click to bind the ID card and add it to the Blaze Banker."
		""
		"Finally, place &6White Card&r into the bottom left slot of the Blaze Banker to bind it. You can then access the account by right clicking a &6Bank Terminal&r with the card."
		""
		"Placing the White Card in your curio slot will allow you to purchase items from villagers using shared funds."
	]
	quest.1F0231C09608265D.title: "Shared Accounts"
	quest.1F12BF72B966E0CC.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of paying the Blacksmith to open &6Geodes&r? Buy the &6Extractinator&r from one!"
		""
		"Right click it with a &6Geode&r to pop it open, free of charge."
	]
	quest.1F12BF72B966E0CC.title: "Free Geode Busting"
	quest.1F23B0E775AD060D.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.1F88FD241787720B.title: "Collection: Brews"
	quest.1FE9F1AD269303B3.quest_desc: ["&6Maglev rails&r have a much higher maximum speed than normal rails."]
	quest.1FFF66E7B3DE1E6D.quest_desc: ["Cook all dishes from &6Farm and Charm&r."]
	quest.1FFF66E7B3DE1E6D.title: "Farm and Charmer"
	quest.2074A4FFF17266DB.title: "Autumn Crops Bundle"
	quest.20F2517A081999C2.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.21671DA370EA7A37.quest_desc: [
		"Unlocking &6Fishing Mastery&r provides special tools for both manual fishing and ponds when unlocked."
		""
		"Once unlocked, the associated items can be bought from the &6Fisher&r."
	]
	quest.2193ACEC05CC5B07.quest_desc: ["&6Construction Wands&r allow you to quickly place blocks in a line or surface. Each tier increases durability, and the amount of blocks that can be placed at a time."]
	quest.2193ACEC05CC5B07.quest_subtitle: "Mass block placement"
	quest.2193ACEC05CC5B07.title: "Building Wands"
	quest.21B07E7D0C412FFA.quest_desc: [
		"Upgraded rods can be equipped with attachments using a &6Tackle Box&r."
		""
		"They will also have a chance to upgrade enchantments from succesful catches. The chance increases on higher upgraded rods."
		""
		"Higher tiers of rods will also increase the size of the minigame bobber!"
	]
	quest.21B07E7D0C412FFA.title: "Upgrading Your Rod"
	quest.21B62899C63D3C4B.title: "Gem Collection Complete!"
	quest.21FD7614E314BA14.title: "Chainmail Armor"
	quest.221306DB217B8F93.quest_desc: [
		"Completing the &6Boiler Room&r will give you the blueprints for mecahanical power. It will give you the power to automate parts of your farm and easily move items around. "
		""
		"&oCreate is not required for progression.&r"
	]
	quest.221306DB217B8F93.title: "Mechanical Farming"
	quest.224AC273D2E3D1D7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Statue of The Moon Gnome&r channels the ancient power of Selene. It can be crafted by a &6Blacksmith&r using Iridium Ingots."
		""
		"Right clicking on it will give you a random mining related Moon Blessing that lasts the entire day."
	]
	quest.2255D3F05F8B895A.title: "Artifact Collection Complete!"
	quest.22E44CB981A4299B.title: "Cooking Collection Complete!"
	quest.230E02067CBC21CF.quest_desc: ["&6Pine Tar&r is tapped from Spruce and Pine trees and is mainly used for advanced farming devices."]
	quest.238702B124895A0A.quest_desc: [
		"If you're not familiar with it, the big list of items in your inventory is known as the &6JEI&r or &6EMI&r panel! While hovering on an item:"
		""
		"&6Left Click/Press R&r to view its recipes"
		"&6Right Click/Press U&r to view its uses"
		""
		"Be sure to check each tab on the top of the recipe, this modpack has many different ways to obtain every item. "
	]
	quest.238702B124895A0A.quest_subtitle: "How to use JEI/EMI"
	quest.238702B124895A0A.title: "Finding Answers!"
	quest.238D909D360FC27C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Deluxe Crab Trap Bait&r improves the chance of catching seafood and treasure from Crab traps, and decreases the chance of junk."
		""
		"The Deluxe Worm Bin upgrades basic &6Crab Trap Bait&r in &61&r day."
	]
	quest.23AF18CF0081AFEF.quest_subtitle: "Nether"
	quest.23BE07D35DAEA28C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Silver&r is another secondary material found in the &6Skull Cavern&r. "
		""
		"It's commonly used in sensitive electronic equipment, and is one of the rarest ores you can find in the cavern."
	]
	quest.23BE07D35DAEA28C.title: "Cavern Metal II"
	quest.23C02B36014CC450.quest_desc: [
		"Can't be bothered to run up to every villager every time you need something??"
		""
		"The &6Phone&r has you covered! Right clicking on it will allow you to select which villager to trade with over the phone. Some shops can only be accessed over the phone!"
		""
		"It is sold by the &6Banker&r Villager."
	]
	quest.23C02B36014CC450.title: "Phone Ordering"
	quest.23EFDF37F9BCD63B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Copycat Blocks&r mimic the texture of the block that you right click with."
		""
		"This can be used to make stairs, ladders, and other variants of blocks that don't have them (e.g concrete blocks)."
		""
		"This also comes in variants that don't normally exist in Minecraft, such as slopes."
	]
	quest.23EFDF37F9BCD63B.title: "Copycat Blocks"
	quest.242D49A4D71EDBEA.quest_desc: [
		"Mining ores in cold biomes or &bWinter&r will have a chance to give you &6Frozen Geodes&r. "
		""
		"Outside of that they can drop from &6Slush&r in cold biomes (affected by fortune), or frozen zombies in &bWinter&r."
	]
	quest.2447ECC5ACB657A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Dragontooth Axe&r can only be wielded if you have the skill &6Dragonslayer&r on the Adventurer skill tree."
		""
		"It's slow, extremely powerful, and does all the things an axe can! "
	]
	quest.24C86673E1F57A3E.quest_desc: [
		"Your farm isn't going to be very successful if you stick to those &6Stone Tools&r..."
		""
		"The &6Carpenter&r can help you build a home for a &6Blacksmith&r. They'll sell you smithing templates to upgrade your tools to iron."
	]
	quest.24C86673E1F57A3E.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Aiden"
	quest.25305BECA3C32315.quest_desc: [
		"Due to the complex world generation of the Skull Cavern, we suggest pre-generating the dimension using Chunky! To do so, run the following commands:"
		""
		"&6/chunky world society:skull_cavern&r"
		"&6/chunky radius 1000&r (increase number for larger servers)"
		"&6/chunky start&r"
		""
		"For additional info on chunky, run &6/chunky help&r"
		""
		"&oIt's best to do this when nobody is online for performance reasons&r"
	]
	quest.25305BECA3C32315.title: "Pregenerating the Skull Cavern"
	quest.25569C0D687E6FA5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Dehydrator&r can be used to dry fruits or vegetables in &61&r day. Fast, but not as profitable as other means."
		""
		"The first one will need to be bought from a &6Market&r, but more can be crafted using &6Raisins&r."
	]
	quest.25677844C218103A.quest_desc: [
		"The day after you reach the maximum level in all of your skill trees, you unlock &6Mastery&r."
		""
		"&6Mastery experience&r is gained from doing most things that gained experience in the base trees like farming crops or catching fish."
		""
		"Once you unlock a skill point in &6Mastery&r, you can pick any of the five. You can unlock all 5 masteries, the choice simply comes down to which one you want sooner. "
	]
	quest.25677844C218103A.quest_subtitle: "Reach level 12 in every skill"
	quest.25677844C218103A.title: "Skill Mastery"
	quest.25777939975C3CEE.quest_desc: [
		"Teleportation does exist, however you will have to invest massive amounts of cash to buy it. "
		""
		"Alternatively, you can build out a network of roads and teleport between them using signs."
	]
	quest.25777939975C3CEE.title: "Transportation"
	quest.25B8A904433E17B3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lead Sheets&r can be processed into &6Sturdy Sheets&r, a stronger material used to make Train related materials."
		""
		"While Trains aren't strictly required for progression, they can be useful for long range transportation or logistical automation."
	]
	quest.25B8A904433E17B3.title: "Intro to Trains"
	quest.25EFF541E1F2C205.title: "Master Sommelier"
	quest.262E7E71CF6AD26A.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.262E7E71CF6AD26A.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.26315E4AC203348C.quest_desc: [
		""
		"The fish you'll catch depends on 4 factors: &aSeason&r, &6Location&r &aWeather&r, and &6Time&r."
		""
		"Each of the four &aseasons&r have their own fish. Each &6location&r (Ocean, River, or Freshwater) has its own pool."
		""
		"Finally, some fish can only be caught during night or day."
	]
	quest.263CCA4D2EAF2629.quest_desc: [
		"When two different Butterflies or Moths are in the same area, they might lay &6Caterpillar Eggs&r!"
		""
		"These are produced using the same mechanics as amber and pollen."
		""
		"The type and size of egg is determined by the closest Butterfly/Moth, and two different parents will produce a third type of butterfly!"
	]
	quest.263CCA4D2EAF2629.title: "Butterfly Breeding!"
	quest.264888DE7B32E80B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Alloy&r is a weaker, but more flexible material used for crafting common mechanical parts."
		""
		"You'll need a lot of it, so it's worth investing in cheaper ways to obtain it. "
	]
	quest.267B2278B71805DD.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.26AF7B63E961DF18.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ender Drawers&r will have the same items available as the drawer linked remotely, no matter the distance. They can be used to transport items easily, but the cost makes them less convenient than they could be."
		""
		"They can be linked using a Linking Card."
	]
	quest.272D9228BC46AEE0.quest_desc: [
		"You've scoured the lands, pillaged the mines, and annoyingly crafted too much food."
		""
		"Doing this insane task is only part of the way towards having the perfect capitalist empire."
	]
	quest.272D9228BC46AEE0.quest_subtitle: "Complete all collections"
	quest.272D9228BC46AEE0.title: "Collectathon"
	quest.2746CBE8BDA47E40.quest_desc: ["&6Diamond Sprinklers&r are far more expensive than the previous tier, but work in a significant area."]
	quest.2777643C0B7C85A7.quest_subtitle: "Crab Traps (Deluxe bait only)"
	quest.28029230D7FD63D6.quest_desc: [
		"Wondering why your tools aren't breaking? All of the main tools and armors have &6infinite&r durability when used."
		""
		"There's one small tradeoff: these tools lose 15%% + 15 durability on death. This only applies to equipment in your hotbar and armor."
		""
		"Tools can be repaired in an anvil infinitely, with significantly lower experience costs. Unbreaking also reduces the amount of durability lost."
	]
	quest.28029230D7FD63D6.quest_subtitle: "Not quite..."
	quest.28029230D7FD63D6.title: "No Durability?"
	quest.28203635739BC73E.quest_desc: [
		"Baits can be added using a &6Tackle Box&r and decrease the amount of time between bites."
		""
		"They are slowly consumed, and better baits such as &6Leeches&r and &6Minnows&r have a higher amount of durability."
	]
	quest.28203635739BC73E.title: "Baiting Fish"
	quest.287FFC7E15278504.quest_desc: [
		"You may notice the tiers of armor and tools have been slightly tweaked."
		""
		"Iron now upgrades to &6Gold&r before &bDiamond&r, adding another step in progression."
		""
		"Unlike vanilla, the &6Gold&r tools are balanced inbetween both tiers."
	]
	quest.287FFC7E15278504.title: "Changed Tiers"
	quest.291360E395E2BA29.quest_desc: ["&6Enriched Bonemeal&r can be used to grow crops such as Glowberries, Lavender, and Hibiscus."]
	quest.29C3F528FEC4D0C7.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.2A02C6E45ED944F4.quest_desc: [
		"Figuring out which Fish can be caught in a given location can be tricky. Some have very specific spawning conditions on top of being very rare."
		""
		"The &6Fish Finder&r lists out every fish in the game and its exact spawn conditions. It can either be found or purchased from a &6Fisher&r."
	]
	quest.2A02C6E45ED944F4.title: "Fishing Guide"
	quest.2A64214504AAD5E5.quest_desc: ["The &6Fisher&r sells fishing rods and addons to upgrade them."]
	quest.2B3BEC36F6C0F6BE.quest_desc: [
		"Oak, Dark Oak, Spruce, and Pine trees can be tapped using a &6Tapper&r. "
		""
		"The type of tree tapped will determine how many days it will take to complete as well as the output."
	]
	quest.2B3BEC36F6C0F6BE.title: "Tapping Wood"
	quest.2B6877708A709B5C.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to &l&6Society: Sunlit Valley&r!"
		""
		"Where farming meets lightly industrialized capitalism."
		""
		"Expand your farming empire and become wealthy in the process."
		""
		"This questbook will give you an introduction to the concepts of the pack, and serve as a journal for collectable items."
	]
	quest.2B6877708A709B5C.quest_subtitle: "You only have to read this one"
	quest.2B6877708A709B5C.title: "Welcome!"
	quest.2C3FD9E2DA520620.quest_desc: [
		"All farm animals require &6Animal Feed&r regularly to produce their products. They need to be fed once every Minecraft day."
		""
		"If an animal goes too long without being fed, they won't be very happy with you..."
	]
	quest.2C3FD9E2DA520620.title: "Raising Animals"
	quest.2C4862DD33189878.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Auto-Petter&r is a rare drop from &6Grimwood Supply Crates&r in the Blackstone Caves."
		""
		"It is a machine filled with ancient power that pets nearby animals every morning, steadily increasing their affection when you're not around. They love it!"
	]
	quest.2C9C87690BD8E23B.quest_desc: [
		"Slimes can be fed in a few ways. The simplest of which is tossing an item they like to eat at them. For Slimes that only eat animals and monsters, you'll need to wrangle one into their area."
		""
		"After being fed, they'll drop a &6Plort&r! These can be sold, used to make more slimes, or processed into more valuable goods!"
	]
	quest.2C9C87690BD8E23B.title: "The Humble Plort"
	quest.2D553026BFCB2CF0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hearthstone&r is an expensive item with limited uses sold by the &6Witch&r that teleports you to your spawn point from anywhere."
		""
		"&oYou can get some extra uses out if it by enchanting it with Unbreaking and Mending.&r"
	]
	quest.2D553026BFCB2CF0.title: "Last Resort"
	quest.2D9AD3D0C59E682B.title: "Collection: Fish"
	quest.2DD84A5F127B1463.quest_desc: [
		"Each sellable item in the pack has one of four categories:"
		""
		"- 🔱 &6Farmer&r - Raw crops and cooked meals"
		"- ✎ &6Artisan&r - Items made in Artisan Machines by hand, such as Preserves, Beer, Wine, Cheese, etc."
		"- 🎣 &6Geologist&r - Ores, gems, and minerals. Anything out of the ground."
		"- 🗡 &6Adventurer&r - Looted artifacts and other rare items."
		""
		"The category is only relevant when it comes to skills, which may increase certain categories if taken."
	]
	quest.2DD84A5F127B1463.title: "Artisan Goods?"
	quest.2E7D98DEB5012260.title: "Slimes Collection Complete!"
	quest.2F83B8F22344FAD7.quest_desc: [
		"The fourth and final layer of the Skull Cavern is made up of the Umbra Barrens and Blackstone Caves. "
		""
		"Both provide a unique set of ores, but you might not have enough time in the day to efficiently mine them."
		""
		"You can also find &6Skull Cavern Teleporters&r down at this layer, allowing you to instantly leave without penalty."
	]
	quest.2F83B8F22344FAD7.title: "Layer IV - The Final Depth"
	quest.3042AA873F9B60C5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Networked Pipes&r are capable of complex logistical operations. They can be used to sort, auto-stock, auto craft, and auto-retrieve items from pipe networks."
		""
		"They require a good bit of skill to use, but the &6Classic Pipes wiki&r online has details for those that wish to master them."
	]
	quest.3042AA873F9B60C5.title: "Complex Logistics"
	quest.3129F3C2D43EE6EE.title: "Crab Trap Bundle"
	quest.314D5DDD65659FDE.title: "Husbandry Bundle"
	quest.318022FDED8803BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6There's no rush in placing villager building blueprints!&r "
		""
		"It can be a ton of work to terraform while trying to build your farm. These blueprints are optional and can always be placed later when you're more established."
		""
		"You can always move the &6Villager Home&r block after placing it."
	]
	quest.318022FDED8803BD.quest_subtitle: "Not enough space..."
	quest.318022FDED8803BD.title: "So many Blueprints!"
	quest.319129CE8210964A.quest_desc: ["&6Iridium&r tools and weapons are the equivalent of &6Netherite&r in vanilla minecraft, with slightly increased attack damage and dig speed."]
	quest.319129CE8210964A.title: "Iridium Tools"
	quest.31F6C5811A72396C.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter lists tools that will help you in building beautiful monuments to capitalism, or quaint farms."
		""
		"As you can imagine, this is all very optional."
	]
	quest.31F6C5811A72396C.title: "Building Tools"
	quest.3211E60DF860BE29.quest_desc: [
		"&6Package Frogports&r will attach packages to &6Chain Conveyers&r to transport items across your base."
		""
		"You'll need a &6Packager&r to turn these items into packages."
		""
		"&oPonder both of these blocks to learn more about package logistics&r"
	]
	quest.3211E60DF860BE29.quest_subtitle: "Package Logistics"
	quest.321F14C492AF6793.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.3291A30C1D1B009D.quest_desc: [
		"The one thing that stands between you and mining wealth is the &6Skull Cavern Teleporter&r."
		""
		"As you mine &6Boulders and Ore&r you'll find ropes going down, taking you to more dangerous and rewarding areas. "
		""
		"&cStaying in the Skull Cavern overnight is dangerous.&r"
		""
		"&c&lYou will faint and be sent home if you're inside it past 5:50 AM.&r"
		""
		"&oBe sure you're absolutely prepared before entering, with enchanted armor and extra hearts..."
	]
	quest.3291A30C1D1B009D.quest_subtitle: "Complete the Vault Bundle"
	quest.3291A30C1D1B009D.title: "The Skull Cavern"
	quest.329C4304D2EDEE72.title: "Frozen Geode Mineral Collection Complete!"
	quest.32A9D7283F680AE3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create Railways Navigator&r is an addon that allows for more detailed display of routes and stations. "
		""
		"Perfect for a server railway."
	]
	quest.32A9D7283F680AE3.title: "Passenger Rails"
	quest.32FE1F4EF913EADA.quest_desc: ["&6Gold&r tools have increased attack damage, dig speed, and durability to &6Iron&r, unlike what you might expect in vanilla Minecraft."]
	quest.32FE1F4EF913EADA.title: "Gold Tools"
	quest.33176CD4D28070D3.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Flamarang&r is the upgraded version of &6Pickarang&r that cannot be destroyed by lava."
		""
		"It also has higher damage and durability."
	]
	quest.33338792EF0994BD.quest_desc: ["Some villagers can only be called over the phone! The &6Banker&r can connect you to these as well as any ones you've unlocked."]
	quest.33338792EF0994BD.title: "Calling Villagers"
	quest.3385C414574E7FE2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Prize Tickets&r can be found as a reward from some harder bounties."
		""
		"Each time you submit one to a &6Prize Machine&r, you'll receive an item. The more you submit, the better the rewards are until it loops."
		""
		"Right click on the &6Prize Machine&r for a hint on the next prize!"
	]
	quest.3385C414574E7FE2.title: "Cool Prizes"
	quest.33BD4404990D4D89.quest_desc: [
		"&6Garden Pots&r grow planted crops indoors during any season, making them a cheap and decorative alternative to &6Greenhouse Glass&r."
		""
		"The catch? Sprinklers can't hydrate them, though Garden Pots will never dry out and break your crop. &6Deluxe Hydrating Fertilizer&r can be used to keep them watered forever."
	]
	quest.33FD69B12C21E495.quest_desc: [
		"&3Neptunium&r can be found from Neptune's Bounty, Crab Traps, and Neptuna."
		""
		"The armors give buffs to underwater movement, breathing, and utility."
	]
	quest.33FD69B12C21E495.title: "Neptunium Armor"
	quest.34206688082CCC57.quest_desc: ["Pickaxes and shovels aren't the only way to mine blocks. These tools are sidegrades for mining that have various effects that make mining easier."]
	quest.34206688082CCC57.title: "Alternative Mining"
	quest.3428ADDC87A77916.quest_desc: [
		"Completing the Boiler Room gives you the &6Kinetic Blueprint&r!"
		""
		"This item allows you to craft power sources for the &6Create&r mod, allowing you to fully automate your farm! "
	]
	quest.3428ADDC87A77916.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Create Power Sources"
	quest.3428ADDC87A77916.title: "Boiler Room Completed!"
	quest.345432E72BD82727.quest_desc: [
		"Manually harvesting from Worm Farms gets old fast. An &6Auto Worm Farm&r cultivates worms in an automatable way, with the added bonus of not needing any inputs!"
		""
		"It can be used to automate Crab Traps, provided you have an automated way to turn Worms into Crab Trap Bait."
	]
	quest.345432E72BD82727.title: "Worm Parade"
	quest.3492FA6A5DFCC390.quest_desc: ["&6Gold Sprinklers&r are a direct upgrade to the iron tier, giving a larger radius."]
	quest.3492FA6A5DFCC390.title: "Gold Sprinklers"
	quest.34AD1E2CEE6966B5.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.34AD1E2CEE6966B5.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.34FCF481CDFD3380.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Bounty Board&r will have bounties requesting different items or tasks done in exchange for coins or other items."
		""
		"Right click a completed bounty on the board to complete."
		""
		"By default it will come with one of four different types of &6Decrees&r, which determine which items will be requested."
	]
	quest.34FCF481CDFD3380.title: "Bounties"
	quest.354AB867025A3019.quest_desc: ["Cinnamon Tree Saplings have a rare chance to drop from &bWinter Zombies&r."]
	quest.354AB867025A3019.quest_subtitle: "&bWinter Zombies"
	quest.35A8A8F8898AE3E5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pristine Quality Fertilizer&r has the highest chance for quality possible."
		""
		"When combined with iridium quality seeds, it practicially garuntees you'll get high quality crops."
	]
	quest.360D17160386D3C4.quest_subtitle: "Crab Traps"
	quest.365B720FB6A9BCF3.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.36ACACFB9D5A97F9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Item Pipes&r transfer items between inventories in easier ways than Mechanical Belts. "
		""
		"You can place them in a line from one inventory to another, then with a Create Wrench &6Shift + Right click&r the pipe that's next to the inventory you want to take items out from."
		""
		"&oPipes also cannot automate Artisan Machines&r"
	]
	quest.36ACACFB9D5A97F9.quest_subtitle: "Get your Strong Allan wrench"
	quest.36ACACFB9D5A97F9.title: "Pipes!"
	quest.3719F024051F60DA.quest_desc: ["&6Truffles&r are valuable goods, found by Pigs when they have at least 5 hearts of affection."]
	quest.376A606EF1F9E850.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.378EF12075D01F1C.title: "Magma Geode Mineral Collection Complete!"
	quest.381A3B258ACE31FD.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.3820DA7C3314E0AD.quest_subtitle: "&6Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.382DC5EBB8C7C19E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blueprints&r can be used to instantly build pre-made buildings, without the need to collect every block!"
		""
		"&6Right Click&r a block with a blueprint to place a preview. Right click again to open the menu."
		""
		"&6Ctrl + Scroll Wheel&r can be used to nudge the blueprint in the direction you scroll."
		""
		"The menu can be used to rotate, mirror, and &6build&r!"
	]
	quest.382DC5EBB8C7C19E.title: "Placing Blueprints"
	quest.3862A7D1A471A215.quest_desc: ["This questline will take you through the basics of the pack to get you started farming."]
	quest.3862A7D1A471A215.title: "The Basics"
	quest.3889A9F0A1CF45FF.title: "Blacksmith's Bundle"
	quest.38A0B8D54F85B846.title: "Diamond Armor"
	quest.38AC25E172172654.quest_desc: [
		"&6Iridium Scrap&r can be combined with &6Bismuth Ingots&r to create &6Iridium Ingots&r, an extremely durable alloy."
		""
		"It can be made into some of the most powerful machinery and armor in the Sunlit Valley. "
	]
	quest.3979B0AD660A33D2.quest_desc: ["Unlocking &6Husbandry Mastery&r allows you to upgrade the production of your animals significantly."]
	quest.3A108FB6BA7E60D6.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.3A1EFD1023C8C09B.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.3A1EFD1023C8C09B.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.3A5DF5AD3C5299DE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Magnifying Glass&r shows the working area of certain blocks using right click (Use while crouching if the block has an inventory)."
		""
		"A list of blocks it works on is in the tooltip when holding shift."
	]
	quest.3B30AFF91D59746A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pickarangs&r can be used to mine at range, bringing drops back for you. "
		""
		"It works on any type of block a Diamond Pickaxe, Shovel, or Axe can."
	]
	quest.3B6640956F047EC8.quest_desc: [
		"Butterflies and Moths produce &6Butterfly Amber&r and &6Moth Pollen&r respectively."
		""
		"The rate is determined by two factors: how many other butterflies and moths are nearby (negatively), and the amount of unique flowers nearby (positively)."
		""
		"Flowers will very occasionally be eaten, requiring a little bit of work to maintain a lush garden of flowers."
	]
	quest.3B6640956F047EC8.title: "The Butterfly Effect"
	quest.3B74A3D3DABA26EF.quest_desc: [
		"Need a bunch of stone blocks for your farm? Look no futher than the &6Mechanical Extruder&r! "
		""
		"It combines liquids on either side into blocks without consuming either one."
	]
	quest.3B74A3D3DABA26EF.title: "Easy Building Blocks"
	quest.3B928722AC96C4B0.title: "Collection: Gems"
	quest.3BC6467B02D74FAC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Small Ships&r allow for traversing the sea quickly. They come in different variants that do better or worse in different ocean biomes."
		""
		"They have large inventories, and can be mounted with cannons or colored with dye."
	]
	quest.3BC6467B02D74FAC.title: "Shipmaking"
	quest.3C0965E47666E5B3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Void Motors&r have the same stress capacity and rotation speed as all other Void Motors in their network. "
		""
		"The network can be configured by setting the frequency using any item."
	]
	quest.3C12A8CA17EACA0B.quest_desc: [
		"Unlocking &6Mining Mastery&r will provide mining riches past your wildest dreams!"
		""
		"The &6Blacksmith&r and &6Trader&r will now help you obtain your mastery equipment, making every mining trip significantly more valuable."
	]
	quest.3C61AB99F40B709F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lead&r is a grating ore that begins to spawn in the frozen layer. When broken, it spawns clouds of brain damage unless adjacent to water."
		""
		"&oThere may be ways to mitigate this risk...&r"
		""
		"Its main use is heavy machinery, particularly in the Create mod."
	]
	quest.3C61AB99F40B709F.title: "Coughing and Spitting"
	quest.3C9A245CFCD5D8E8.quest_desc: [
		"Wines can be made with three fruits and even certain vegetables in a &6Wine Keg&r."
		""
		"This process is lengthy, but much more profitable per-fruit than preserving."
	]
	quest.3CF0897E67574877.quest_desc: ["The &6Shepherd&r can get you started with animals on your farm, selling &6Animal Feed&r as well as spawn crates of some basic farm animals."]
	quest.3D324E99DF28D224.quest_desc: [
		"Farm animals require love and attention! They can be pet once a day with an added bonus if you feed them by hand."
		""
		"Cramped conditions where more than 6 or so animals are walled in or packed together will make them lose happiness."
		""
		"Right click a farm animal with an empty hand to see their affection."
	]
	quest.3D324E99DF28D224.title: "Affection"
	quest.3D532DC93531B0D0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Crafters&r are automatable Crafting Tables that have a few exclusive recipes. "
		""
		"&oLocometal Boilers take up a large amount of pages in JEI. The second task shows all of the available ones.&r"
	]
	quest.3DE36C9FBCB58800.quest_desc: [
		"Entering the Nether will catch the eye of a &6Witch&r!"
		""
		"You'll be able to purchase special magical equipment for a high price, most noteworthy being &6Crystals of Regret&r."
	]
	quest.3DE36C9FBCB58800.quest_subtitle: "Inviting Evelyne"
	quest.3DE36C9FBCB58800.title: "Magic in the Valley"
	quest.3E074A7E5B773419.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sharestones&r can teleport you to any of the same color. All 4 are needed to attain perfection."
		""
		"&oYou don't have to read the other Sharestone quests.&r"
	]
	quest.3E08F21BA8F69499.quest_desc: [
		"Strengthening your bond with the villagers will make them feel more at home in your town!"
		""
		"&6Shift + Right Click&r on a villager to give them a gift once every 4 days."
		""
		"Things that have a sell value are always giftable, but you can find the full list by searching &6#villager_gift&r in JEI/EMI."
	]
	quest.3E08F21BA8F69499.title: "Giving Gifts"
	quest.3E48E03F3F044FF2.quest_desc: ["Baits can be added using a &6Tackle Box&r and have various effects on your rod."]
	quest.3E48E03F3F044FF2.title: "Fishing Hooks"
	quest.3E4F57BA2601FD6F.quest_desc: [
		"Animals are sensitive to changes in their care or environment. They may really like you, but if you mistreat them it'll effect their produce!"
		""
		"You can check how an animal is feeling by right clicking them with an empty hand. "
		""
		"- Smiles (☺) indicate the animal is happy! They'll produce quality items."
		"- Frowns (☹) indicate the animal is sad, giving them a chance to not produce that day."
		""
		"You can get detailed information on an animal's mood by right clicking them with the &6Mood Scanner&r purchased from the Shepherd."
	]
	quest.3E4F57BA2601FD6F.title: "Animal Mood"
	quest.3E57558B04952D59.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.3E57558B04952D59.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.3EF57F71C1C786FE.title: "Summer Crops Bundle"
	quest.3F759C6DEEBC61FD.quest_desc: [
		"To get started making money, you'll need a &6Basic Shipping Bin&r."
		""
		"Items placed inside that have a sell value will be sold at &66 AM&r for the value listed in the tooltip."
	]
	quest.3F759C6DEEBC61FD.title: "Making Money"
	quest.3FA607115DB107D9.quest_desc: [
		"The third layer will greatly test your ability to survive. You'll start to encounter &6Iridium Scrap&r, &6Silver&r, and a variety of deadly new enemies that can efficiently kill you."
		""
		"If you're struggling to survive here, you should focus on getting better gear. "
		""
		"In particular, things that will allow you to get around faster like hooks and attack from range like bows will be key."
	]
	quest.3FA607115DB107D9.title: "Layer III - The Deep Desert"
	quest.3FC4155A11F14663.title: "Elementium Armor"
	quest.3FF6591FC54809B1.quest_subtitle: "&6Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.4041362E384D0744.quest_subtitle: "&6Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.40845F4C88AD03CB.quest_desc: ["Unlocking &6Farming Mastery&r will give you powerful new plants to grow on your farm that can be obtained from the &6Market&r using &6Prismatic Shards&r."]
	quest.4092A4464F986217.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Auto-Cheese Press&r is an automated version of the &6Artisan Cheese Press&r. Hoppers can be used to insert and extract out of it."
		""
		"Unlike the base version, it requires &6Rennet&r for the production of cheeses and does not carry over quality. "
	]
	quest.4092A4464F986217.title: "Automated Cheese"
	quest.40AD1233DF08EBCC.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Aging Cask&r ages items over large periods of time, multiplying their sell value by &64&r."
		""
		"Wine will take take &610&r days to age, while other items like Beer, Whisky, and Cheese take a shorter amount of time."
	]
	quest.40C8DC3C2A22F632.quest_desc: [
		"Now that your pets are ready to adventure with you, the &6Guild&r will now sells supplies to keep them safe."
		""
		"Most notable is the &6Pet Bed&r, which allows your pets to respawn if they somehow lose the battle. "
		""
		"Make sure you see the ZZZs above the pet's bed after placing them there!"
	]
	quest.40C8DC3C2A22F632.title: "Pet Utilities"
	quest.41029F073ADDDC2F.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Slime&r will drop a different type of &6Plort&r when fed a food in their diet. The humble &dSlimy Slimes&r will eat berries, but more advanced Slimes will have higher standards. You can tell a Slime's diet by hovering over it in world."
		""
		"Each slime has a favorite food that will cause them to drop double Plorts."
		""
		"The &6Plort Rippit&r can be used to turn Plorts into various resources depending on the breed."
	]
	quest.41029F073ADDDC2F.title: "Rippit!"
	quest.410784379F435E05.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Witch&r now sells the &6Enchanting Table&r. This will allow you to unlock the final level for enchantments such as Fortune or Looting, alongside enchantments that aren't included in the skill tree."
		""
		"The maximums of enchantments that are in the skill tree has been lowered!"
	]
	quest.41C453E806763C4F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Trader&r villager sells machine upgrades for various farm goods. These upgrades add special effects when applied to the machine."
		""
		"There are also some handy utility trades for useful but annoying to obtain items, such as Wither Skeleton Skulls."
	]
	quest.41C453E806763C4F.title: "Machine Upgrades"
	quest.41FD632FA78AFB49.quest_desc: [
		"In order to channel the power of lightning, a large amount of &6Blaze Rods&r will be needed. "
		""
		"They can be found in the traditional way by killing Blazes, but can also be found embedded in some ores."
		""
		"Aim for at least &67&r of them."
	]
	quest.41FD632FA78AFB49.title: "Harnessing Fire"
	quest.429FEBEC239B975F.quest_desc: [
		"Fish are a fast and valuable way to make money early game."
		""
		"Your first rod will come from the &6Fisher&r villager, and they otherwise sell aquatic and fishing related supplies."
	]
	quest.429FEBEC239B975F.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Haruna"
	quest.429FEBEC239B975F.title: "Fishing"
	quest.42A10CEE57513522.quest_desc: [
		"Signs can be used to fast travel provided a well made path is between them."
		""
		"Use a &6Charting Map&r to start and finish charting, adding signs to the path by right clicking them."
		""
		"You can search &6#path_block&r in JEI to see all the valid path blocks."
	]
	quest.42A10CEE57513522.quest_subtitle: "Accessibile Instant Teleportation"
	quest.42A10CEE57513522.title: "Paving the Road"
	quest.42B424793E1E91D3.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fish Pond Basket&r is a machine powered by &dSparkstone&r that can automate collection from adjacent &6Fish Ponds&r!"
		""
		"It requires sparkstone in its inventory and an inventory below it to deposit items."
	]
	quest.42BBE95A6DE1DD19.quest_desc: [
		"Many recipes in this pack are modified or require currency. "
		""
		"Like games such as Stardew Valley and Harvest Moon, exploit the earth for profit!"
	]
	quest.42BBE95A6DE1DD19.title: "Shipping and Currency"
	quest.42C8E1F0D9A5B2BD.quest_desc: [
		"By now your storage situation may be getting dire. Thankfully the &6Librarian&r villager sells tools for sorting your base out."
		""
		"At the end of every season, you'll also have access to the &6Book fair&r, a special shop that sells different skill books."
	]
	quest.42C8E1F0D9A5B2BD.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Veronica"
	quest.43591809C1D493F5.quest_desc: ["Gold quality crops only. Only &63&r tasks required for bundle completion."]
	quest.43591809C1D493F5.title: "Quality Bundle"
	quest.43C52E202277C5AA.title: "Stone Tools"
	quest.44256671D7500BEA.quest_desc: ["Cook all dishes from &6Farmer's Delight&r, &6Crabber's Delight&r, &6Veggies's Delight&r and &6Vintage Delight&r."]
	quest.44256671D7500BEA.title: "Delightful Darling"
	quest.449B0ECBBD4E743D.quest_desc: ["Fruit tree sapling a possible reward from a &5Prize Machine&r."]
	quest.449B0ECBBD4E743D.quest_subtitle: "&5Prize Machine"
	quest.44A512703C4A9990.quest_desc: [
		"By now, your farm should have enough tools in order to make a steady income. Your next step should be unlocking the Skull Cavern."
		""
		"[\"\",TRANSLATION_ERROR}]"
		""
		"The rewards on their own will make up for the cost."
	]
	quest.44A512703C4A9990.title: "Making Real Money"
	quest.44ACDBB4DE598EA6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Recycling Machine&r can turn items that would otherwise be junk into useful materials."
		""
		"It can also double the amount of ores you receive from raw ore!"
	]
	quest.44ACDBB4DE598EA6.title: "Trash To Treasure"
	quest.44C829CA1FB1673A.quest_subtitle: "Skull Cavern"
	quest.45120BEE01BB36B4.quest_desc: [
		"This will likely be your first and easiest stop to attaining perfection, but it's one you cannot skip."
		""
		"Completing each room has its own rewards and merits."
	]
	quest.45120BEE01BB36B4.quest_subtitle: "Complete all Bundles"
	quest.45120BEE01BB36B4.title: "Rebuilder"
	quest.4513A91DA55E8069.quest_desc: [
		"&6Small Ships&r can be crafted using &6Artisan Canvas&r, allowing quicker sailing through the ocean. By default, the &6R&r hotkey can be used to drop the sail."
		""
		"These can be used to transport large amounts of exotic farm animals from far away lands."
	]
	quest.4513A91DA55E8069.title: "Set Sail"
	quest.455F9A4D9B1FF43E.quest_desc: ["The seed for &bAncient Fruit&r is found from a variety of sources... But you'll need to figure that out for yourself."]
	quest.455F9A4D9B1FF43E.quest_subtitle: "???"
	quest.4564673A6912E917.quest_desc: [
		"Mining Sandstone and lower types of &6Boulders&r in the Skull Cavern has a small chance to yield &6Iridium Scrap&r. The lower you dive, the higher the chance it drops."
		""
		"&oYou may even find Iridium Ore at the lowest levels...&r"
	]
	quest.45739CCE73037CBB.quest_desc: [
		"Birds such as Chickens will produce eggs, but won't produce them as fast when at lower levels of affection."
		""
		"They'll produce larger eggs at high levels of affection."
	]
	quest.45739CCE73037CBB.title: "Eggs"
	quest.4575948F05E18615.quest_desc: [
		"&6Precision Mechanisms&r are technological marvels that act as the \"brain\" of complex machinery."
		""
		"&6Gold Coins&r are the perfect size and shape for such device, placed alongside normal cogs on a Silver Sheet. "
	]
	quest.4575948F05E18615.title: "Delicate Parts"
	quest.458EC4BFA0C47FCB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Market&r will trade a &6Mystic Willow Sapling&r, which can be tapped for its valuable syrup."
		""
		"You'll first need the rare &6Grimwood sapling&r, found in the world or rarely dug up from harvesting crops. "
	]
	quest.458EC4BFA0C47FCB.title: "Purple Syrup"
	quest.459BA5CC983CFAB9.quest_desc: [
		"There are 5 skill trees that can be leveled, unlocking special abilities useful to you. You can view these trees using &6K&r by default."
		""
		"&6Farming&r experience comes from harvesting crops, eating cooked meals, and using Artisan Machines (such as Preserves Jars or Looms)."
		""
		"&6Husbandry&r experience comes from taking care of animals."
		""
		"&6Mining&r experience comes from mining ores and Geode Nodes, provided you aren't using Silk Touch."
		""
		"&6Fishing&r experience comes from catching fish, crafting fishing equipment, and harvesting from Fish Ponds."
		""
		"&6Adventuring&r experience comes from killing mobs and especially from looting chests."
	]
	quest.459BA5CC983CFAB9.title: "Skills and Levels"
	quest.45BFBE39B1F664B2.quest_subtitle: "Skull Cavern"
	quest.45D9A962F73792EA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Item Pipes&r are handy, but relatively slow to move items around, and don't have the filtering properties of Brass."
		""
		"The &6Advanced Pipe Upgrade&r can be inserted into an extracting pipe to increase the amount of items moved at once. It also unlocks complex filtering options."
		""
		"You can also set the destination of items in complex pipe networks using the &6Filter Destination Tool&r."
	]
	quest.4622E3EC44CED1B6.quest_desc: [
		"Sunlit Valley offers many transportation options for the many types of players."
		""
		"This page lists all the options for getting around your world."
	]
	quest.4622E3EC44CED1B6.title: "Transportation Options"
	quest.4633C0427ACA18D3.quest_desc: ["The &6Banker&r sells management tools to make handling your finances easier."]
	quest.469CEB4C8B3C0EA9.quest_desc: ["Completeting the Fish Tank gives you the &3Neptunium-Infused Hook&r. This can be added to your rod to give you higher luck and a chance to catch &6Relic Troves&r."]
	quest.469CEB4C8B3C0EA9.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Neptunium-Infused Hook"
	quest.469CEB4C8B3C0EA9.title: "Fish Tank Completed!"
	quest.472A339723DE2777.quest_desc: [
		"Placing a &6Tapper&r on an &6Acacia&r tree will yield &6Sap&r the next day."
		""
		"This can be smelted into &6Rubber&r, a key resource for Create used in Belts, Funnels, and other items."
	]
	quest.472A339723DE2777.title: "Industrially Crafted Rubber"
	quest.472F40ECF199DD42.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike vanilla Minecraft, crops need water to grow, and farmland won't be hydrated from nearby water!"
		""
		"They can be watered using a &6Watering Can&r, which will need to be done every day."
		""
		"Every morning at &66 AM&r, farmland will dry up and crops will grow on your farm. If the farmland is dry, your crops will die!"
	]
	quest.472F40ECF199DD42.title: "Watering Crops"
	quest.473D0A5E8D57CD4B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mushroom Soil&r grows mushroom colonies when mushrooms are planted on them."
		""
		"When the colonies are broken, they drop a handful of mushrooms, allowing for farming them."
	]
	quest.4759B2BFFF26E78F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Artisan Hopper&r is a machine powered by &dSparkstone&r that can automate collection from adjacent &6Artisan Machines&r!"
		""
		"Items placed in the inventory above it will automatically be inserted into nearby Artisan Machines that can take those items, no filtering needed!"
		""
		"It requires sparkstone in its inventory and an inventory below it to deposit items."
	]
	quest.4759B2BFFF26E78F.quest_subtitle: "Now in Mini form!"
	quest.47CF88FE788DD872.title: "Collection: Artifacts"
	quest.47DE6A5A64755084.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.48C83D8D34DBFB4B.quest_desc: ["&6Void Steel&r is an optional alloy of Iridium and Eye of Ender. It's used to craft machines fueled by ender power for teleportation."]
	quest.48C83D8D34DBFB4B.title: "Steel of Ender"
	quest.48F1059FC059D3E5.quest_desc: [
		"All armor must start off with a leather or wool base."
		""
		"Wool clothing can also be sewn if you can aquire a &6Sewing Table&r from a &6Market&r villager"
	]
	quest.48F1059FC059D3E5.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.49477F09DF6EBA50.quest_desc: ["The &6Librarian&r sells equipment for managing your storage, including the &6Refined Storage system&r to digitally store your items."]
	quest.49477F09DF6EBA50.title: "Librarian"
	quest.499871FDD2A65F2C.quest_desc: ["The &6Blacksmith&r sells metals, smithing templates, and &6Geode Busters&r for cracking open geodes."]
	quest.4A4474120CD64CBD.quest_desc: [
		"The &6DIY Workbench&r crafts any Furniture Catalog item for a very low material cost."
		""
		"It is also excruciatingly and unnecessarily expensive."
	]
	quest.4A4474120CD64CBD.quest_subtitle: "The Money Sink"
	quest.4A48308E11476E9B.quest_desc: [
		"&3Neptunium&r is a precious material used in crafting advanced fishing gear."
		""
		"It can be found in &3Neptune's Bounty&r you fish up, or rarely in Crab Traps."
	]
	quest.4A708E01E3A3B8D3.title: "Complete the Abandoned Farm"
	quest.4A96DC00D7D0CAD6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Silver Ore&r is an elusive ore that starts to spawn in the third layer."
		""
		"It is used in mass quantities for delicate electronics in &6Create&r, but otherwise is used decoratively. "
	]
	quest.4ABFC024D15BFC10.quest_desc: [
		"Slimes cannot reproduce by breeding. Instead, their &6Plorts&r must be pressed into another &6Slime Heart&r using a &6Plort Press&r."
		""
		"Hearts can also be combined to make new ones using the top and bottom slots."
	]
	quest.4ABFC024D15BFC10.title: "Pressit!"
	quest.4B9634D942E590AB.quest_desc: [
		"Purchasing the Vault gives you a &6Skull Cavern Teleporter&r, your gateway to obtaining &dPrismatic Shards&r."
		""
		"Place it down and right click to enter, but be sure to come prepared! Mobs in the Skull Cavern have twice as much health and damage..."
		""
		"&oThe &6Skull Cavern Teleporter&r&o can also be bought from the &6Guild&r&o if it is lost somehow."
	]
	quest.4B9634D942E590AB.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Skull Cavern Teleporter"
	quest.4B9634D942E590AB.title: "Vault Completed!"
	quest.4BC9FE01DC8D5ADB.quest_desc: ["The &6Potato Cannon&r uses air in your backtank to launch vegetables at dangerous velocity."]
	quest.4BC9FE01DC8D5ADB.quest_subtitle: "Shooting your shot"
	quest.4C2120EC29BE0E64.quest_desc: ["&6Iridium&r armors are the equivalent of &6Netherite&r in vanilla minecraft, with slightly increased protection."]
	quest.4C2120EC29BE0E64.title: "Iridium Armor"
	quest.4C9E6CB01631C0B6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Powdered Obsidian&r is a byproduct of crushing Obsidian using a pair of &6Crushing Wheels&r. It is the final resource needed for advanced farming machinery. "
		""
		"&oIt can also be used to cut lead, turning Lead Ingots into more Molten Lead than they're originally worth.&r"
	]
	quest.4C9E6CB01631C0B6.title: "Sturdy Dust"
	quest.4CE5E17948C31E2A.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.4CE5E17948C31E2A.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.4D00DF575B8FC1B2.title: "Ocean Fish Bundle"
	quest.4D1F2652FD9DEF69.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Auto-Grabber&r is a machine powered by &dSparkstone&r that can automate collection from husbandry farm animals!"
		""
		"Unlike Create Deployers, these devices use any Husbandry skills you might have unlocked, and animals don't lose happiness from harvesting!"
		""
		"It requires sparkstone in its inventory and an inventory below it to deposit items."
		""
		"It can be upgraded with Magic Shears to automatically harvest meat, though this does reduce their affection if they aren't pet every day."
	]
	quest.4DB169DA4B4CCFBA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Banker&r can provide you with tools that make managing your money significantly easier."
		""
		"You'll need to invite a &6Market&r villager to purchase this invitation."
	]
	quest.4DB169DA4B4CCFBA.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Caroline"
	quest.4DC073ABF3D72467.quest_desc: [
		"The Butterfly \\& Moth handbook provides information on where to find every single variant that exists."
		""
		"The spawning of specific variants is determined by the current biome's &6Temperature&r and &6Humidity&r."
		""
		"It also acts as a way to view your collection outside of the quest book, though it needs to be in your inventory for every catch."
	]
	quest.4DC073ABF3D72467.title: "The Handbook"
	quest.4E5BF157FDA7490A.quest_desc: ["Infused with the energy of &dSparkstone&r, the &6Cornucopia&r causes nearby fruit trees to drop their fruits in a large radius around you when used."]
	quest.4E5BF157FDA7490A.title: "Easier Fruit Tree Harvesting"
	quest.4EA02089CD02F7C0.quest_desc: [
		"&3Neptunium&r can be found from Neptune's Bounty, Crab Traps, and Neptuna."
		""
		"The tools typically remove the underwater mining penalty, and weapons deal more damage underwater."
	]
	quest.4EA02089CD02F7C0.title: "Neptunium Tools"
	quest.4EAA3F652AE923B4.quest_desc: ["The &6Trowel&r places blocks in your hotbar randomly. Good for paving long paths of gravel and stone!"]
	quest.4EAA3F652AE923B4.title: "Random Placement"
	quest.4EFD1F876D69591E.quest_desc: ["&6Backtanks&r can be charged with air via create rotation, and store air that can be used to breathe underwater while wearing a diving helmet."]
	quest.4EFD1F876D69591E.quest_subtitle: "Deep sea diving"
	quest.4EFD1F876D69591E.title: "Pneumatic Equipment"
	quest.4F54E885ECC26922.quest_desc: ["The &6Blaze Hook&r is a direct upgrade in speed, but only has two hooks. It also sets mobs on fire if they pass through the hook chain."]
	quest.4F698E7353FD76F1.quest_desc: [
		"Batteries are needed to craft the &6Espresso Machine&r, which lets you make &6Espresso&r and &6Steamed Milk&r."
		""
		"Unlike other Artisan Machines, drinks made with &6Espresso&r are 🔱 Farmer products."
	]
	quest.4F7FB7C8808AF152.quest_desc: [
		"Shaders come pre-installed!"
		""
		"Press &6o&r to enable, provided your PC has the specs capable for them."
	]
	quest.4F7FB7C8808AF152.title: "Shaders?"
	quest.4FE455E397B5E65D.quest_desc: [
		"With so many materials coming from tapping trees, a basic Tapper won't cut it. The &6Auto-Tapper&r is an alternative option, allowing you to pump out the tapped fluid from the bottom of the block."
		""
		"Tapped fluids need to either be bottled or used directly."
	]
	quest.4FE455E397B5E65D.title: "Auto-Tapping"
	quest.501D5F9B05EF9B3F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Chain Conveyers&r transport rotational energy over longer distances."
		""
		"They can also be ridden by right clicking with a &6Wrench&r!"
	]
	quest.501D5F9B05EF9B3F.title: "Long Distance Power"
	quest.505BE1C2FA826879.quest_desc: ["Items used in the storage and movement of fluids can be crafted from Copper, with Oak Resin as a sealing agent."]
	quest.505BE1C2FA826879.title: "Fluid Movement"
	quest.505C0E636F881791.quest_desc: [
		"&6Animal Crackers&r are mystical foods that allow farm animals to produce double when eaten by one. "
		""
		"They can be found randomly throughout the world from your daily farming activities."
	]
	quest.506B32619EB8477F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Advanced Wine Keg&r offers more complex but faster winemaking."
		""
		"It can produce wines far faster than its based version, but requires juice from grapes to speed up the fermentation process."
		""
		"&oIt can also be automated without the need for Sparkstone.&r"
	]
	quest.5108E61542739DFC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Void Tanks&r have the same fluid available in its tank to all other Void Tanks in their network. "
		""
		"The network can be configured by setting the frequency using any item."
	]
	quest.51113C6989787678.quest_subtitle: "Skull Cavern"
	quest.514F85795846913A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Saws&r fell trees in a single swoop automatically. They can be used in contraptions to automate the collection of logs."
		""
		"Once crafted, they can be duplicated using a cheaper recipe."
	]
	quest.51772B6C1CD5DD1E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mossberries&r are the jewels of &6Autumn&r!"
		""
		"They rarely grow on trees and drop when chopped. "
		""
		"Unlike other berries, they cannot be farmed like crops. "
	]
	quest.51772B6C1CD5DD1E.title: "Autumn Tree Berry"
	quest.51CCE1E8F9C7560A.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.523925A720130B12.quest_desc: [
		"Have a large train network? Are you on a large server and constantly getting lost with the amount of train stations?"
		""
		"The &6Create Railways Navigator&r can help guide you, automatically planning routes and transfers to your selected destination."
	]
	quest.527F7721ED60868C.quest_desc: [
		"There are 3 advanced tiers of &6Coins&r. The first two can be crafted up or down from the previous &dPrismatic Coins&r must be traded using a &6Bankers&r,"
		""
		"These are their values:"
		""
		"- Neptunium (&632,768&r) "
		"- Ancient (&6262,144&r)"
		"- Prismatic (&616,252,928&r)"
		""
		"These coins are needed for very late game items. Don't expect to need them anytime soon."
	]
	quest.527F7721ED60868C.title: "Higher Tiers"
	quest.52A3D52D6251EDB6.title: "Geologist's Bundle"
	quest.52A790F80019F520.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hyper Fertilizer&r is the fastest and most expensive of them all, shortening grow times by 3 days."
		""
		"It can be used for painfully slow growing crops, or to make quickly growing crops a daily harvest."
	]
	quest.52F1DCA9462F825F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Witch&r has a deep connection with the nature of the valley and sells various expensive and magical goods."
		""
		"she can be invited after visiting the &6Nether&r for the first time."
	]
	quest.52F1DCA9462F825F.title: "Witch"
	quest.530890B3F0CE32B1.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.530890B3F0CE32B1.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.531CCAEFB0498F98.title: "Collection: Crops"
	quest.53836B96EE81A695.quest_desc: [
		"Create Trains are the ultimate form of railway transport, allowing you to build large custom locomotives with multiple cars."
		""
		"Tracks and Train gear can be crafted without Create Progression!"
		""
		"They can also be automated using &6Train Schedules&r to transport items and fluids."
	]
	quest.53836B96EE81A695.title: "Advanced Trains"
	quest.5384CAC9635C71E5.quest_desc: [
		"Grape juice in liquid form can be easily put inside of Advanced Wine Kegs using the &6Juice Inserter&r."
		""
		"Pump liquids in and they will continually provide juice fluids."
	]
	quest.5384CAC9635C71E5.title: "Automated Juice Logistics"
	quest.53C771625381F8F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lead&r is a sturdy enough material to build trains in your world!"
		""
		"Unlike what you may be used to, trains from Create do not require create progress or power."
		""
		""
		"[\"\",TRANSLATION_ERROR}]"
	]
	quest.54301E900FFA56D7.title: "Diamond Tools"
	quest.5447B467AA6BA5F2.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.546AA268840CA5B3.quest_desc: [
		"Beds can keep you stuck in one place to avoid losing your home. "
		""
		"The &6Sleeping Bag&r solves this by allowing you to sleep away the night while not setting your spawn."
	]
	quest.546AA268840CA5B3.title: "Sleep Anywhere"
	quest.54780E956DA9AB08.quest_subtitle: "Overworld Structures"
	quest.54B5FB32B885916A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Bottler&r is a &6Packager&r but for fluids!"
		""
		"It can be attached to a &6Fluid Tank&r and transported in the same way a package can."
	]
	quest.54B5FB32B885916A.title: "Fluid Logistics"
	quest.54B618CF0AB9DC20.quest_desc: [
		"Watering your crops every morning gets old fast."
		""
		"&6Sprinklers&r help you out by keeping farmland hydrated in a radius around them."
		""
		"The basic Iron tier works in a 3x3 area centered around it."
		""
		"They can also be right clicked with a stick to add support for decoration."
	]
	quest.54B6F31A66A23AD4.quest_desc: [
		"The blueprinting system used for the Building Shop can also be used to make your own blueprints!"
		""
		"The &6Scanner&r is used to capture a build."
		""
		"The &6Tablet&r is used to obtain blueprints to use, or share them with other players."
		""
		"You can use this to plan builds in creative first!"
	]
	quest.54B6F31A66A23AD4.title: "Blueprints"
	quest.54E81642A0E67042.quest_desc: [
		"Slimes can be fed by tossing their food on the ground, or Providing a live mob for them to eat."
		""
		"This can be done in a more convenient way with the &6Slime Feeder&r, which feeds nearby Slimes with foods from their diet."
		""
		"Additionally, if a Slime has the \"Picky\" trait, the Slime Feeder will only feed the food item that won't make it angry."
	]
	quest.54E81642A0E67042.title: "Feeding Slimes"
	quest.54E8CF90BE620790.title: "Complete the Crafts Room"
	quest.5558DB4DE54C890D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ancient Fruit&r is an extremely valuable farmland crop with a long growing time."
		""
		"Upgrading a &6Seed Maker&r with an &6Ancient Cog&r will give you a chance to get its seed with every harvest."
	]
	quest.5558DB4DE54C890D.title: "Cogs of the Ancients"
	quest.55A3F4C2B6F3460B.quest_desc: ["&6Mining Dynamite&r is highly efficient at breaking stone, dropping all the items on the ground at the point of contact."]
	quest.55D658B5939D9DEB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Wireless Crafting Grid&r allows you to access your storage network from a distance!"
		""
		"You'll also need to purchase a &6Wireless Transmitter&r and place it somewhere on your network. Multiple can be added at different areas of your base to cover a wider area!"
		""
		"Alternatively, their range can be extended with &6Range Upgrades&r."
	]
	quest.55D658B5939D9DEB.title: "Wireless Access"
	quest.55F17BB945CA5BB2.quest_desc: ["The &6Guild&r will help you on your adventures, selling tools to navigate around the world better."]
	quest.55FAFBCDEDDA41A5.quest_desc: ["&6Treated Logs&r can be made by right clicking Oak Resin onto any Log in world."]
	quest.562817C23134A26D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Magic Mirror&r teleports you to your spawn point provided it is in range."
		""
		"The range can be upgraded, and works cross-dimensionally."
		""
		"It is a reward for completing the &6Crafts Room&r."
	]
	quest.5629152AF2F5D6EE.title: "16,384 Bundle"
	quest.56865D2E8C786C7D.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.56865D2E8C786C7D.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.5704D9E5E98945DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Windmills&r are slower, and less space efficient than Water Wheels. Their main advantage is looking pretty and requiring less Lead per unit of stress."
		""
		"The more &6Windmill Sails&r connected to a &6Windmill Bearing&r, the higher the stress output."
	]
	quest.5704D9E5E98945DF.title: "Wind Power"
	quest.572D70993411EA53.quest_desc: [
		"&6Organic Mash&r is difficult to come by, but grows any type of crop instantly. It is a byproduct of producing &6Vinegar&r."
		""
		"It can be used to instantly grow crops, as well as growing small mushrooms into larger ones. "
	]
	quest.574978CE534E254B.quest_desc: ["The &6Abacus&r measures the distance between two blocks using right click."]
	quest.574978CE534E254B.title: "Measuring Blocks"
	quest.580FA272625D0922.quest_subtitle: "&6Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.5837B77D1243D30F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Gadgets&r can be used to create, exchange, copy, and destroy portions of the world."
		""
		"They are extremely powerful once you learn how to use them, but the UI may be confusing to newcomers. &6Gadgets for Derps&r explains how to use them in detail."
	]
	quest.5875FF0D35A7E422.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sharestones&r can teleport you to any of the same color. All 4 are needed to attain perfection."
		""
		"&oYou don't have to read the other Sharestone quests.&r"
	]
	quest.58FB1A6006C36FD8.quest_desc: [
		"The fishing minigame can be turned on and off at any time using the command:"
		""
		"&6/stardew_fishing toggle_minigame&r"
		""
		"You won't be able to catch quality fish or get extra treasure, but those can both be obtained using other methods!"
	]
	quest.58FB1A6006C36FD8.title: "Don't like the minigame?"
	quest.596D2298299CCEED.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Farmer's Almanac&r has detailed information of crops and farm animals, which is essential when deciding what to focus on every season."
		""
		"It is sold by the &6Market&r and &6Shepherd&r"
	]
	quest.596D2298299CCEED.title: "All on Farming"
	quest.597C843B42219362.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.5A0AA87EA971F13F.quest_desc: [
		"Build highways around your world lined with fields of corn, the true capitalist dream."
		""
		"The &6Auto Mechanic Table&r can be used to make car parts that are then assembled on an &6Automobile Assembler&r."
		""
		"&oOff-road wheels recommended&r"
	]
	quest.5A0AA87EA971F13F.title: "Cars"
	quest.5A3012C1FA5184A2.quest_desc: [
		"Like the description suggests, striking your &6Hearthstone&r with lightning will allow it to be bound to a single location. Outside of that, it has the same exact properties as before."
		""
		"This can easily be done with a &6Charging Rod&r during a storm."
	]
	quest.5A3012C1FA5184A2.title: "Enhanced Stone"
	quest.5A369FC904BCF5EE.quest_desc: [
		"The one thing that stands between you and mining wealth is the &6Skull Cavern Teleporter&r."
		""
		"As you mine &6Boulders and Ore&r you'll find ropes going down, taking you to more dangerous and rewarding areas. "
		""
		"&cStaying in the Skull Cavern overnight is dangerous.&r"
		""
		"&c&lYou will faint and be sent home if you're inside it past 5:50 AM.&r"
	]
	quest.5A369FC904BCF5EE.quest_subtitle: "Complete the Vault Bundle"
	quest.5A369FC904BCF5EE.title: "The Skull Cavern"
	quest.5A9808F763A6B9F8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Blunderbuss&r is a ranged mechanical firearm intended for hunting monsters and balloons. "
		""
		"It has no charging time, making it perfect for dangerous areas such as the &6Skull Cavern&r."
	]
	quest.5A9808F763A6B9F8.quest_subtitle: "Not very cottagecore of you..."
	quest.5A9808F763A6B9F8.title: "Mechanical Firepower"
	quest.5AD7C2BCDA001A53.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Canvas Loom&r is an artisan machine for making &6Artisan Canvas&r and &6Merino Wool&r in &61&r day."
		""
		"These products can either be sold, crafted into useful items, or sewn into clothing using a &6Sewing Table&r."
	]
	quest.5B2FC6D0E6C24D83.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5B2FC6D0E6C24D83.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.5B5A764F0E02E5FF.quest_desc: [
		"Cows, Sheep, Goats, Wooly Cows, and Water Buffalos can all be milked."
		""
		"Milking animals requires a special &6Milk Pail&r for collection."
		""
		"The size of the milk will depend on how much the animal likes you!"
	]
	quest.5B5A764F0E02E5FF.title: "Milk"
	quest.5B6FD08D6063D6AA.quest_desc: [
		"Bundles are the first large goal of the pack. They require certain items to be submitted, giving small rewards for each bundle, and large rewards when all bundles are completed."
		""
		"The most important right now is:"
		""
		"[\"\",TRANSLATION_ERROR}]"
		""
		"Consisting of products that can grow on your farm."
	]
	quest.5BAFB04B1F3B8150.quest_desc: ["To progress further, you'll need to press ingots into sheets using a &6Mechanical Press&r."]
	quest.5BAFB04B1F3B8150.title: "Ex-Press-O"
	quest.5C6688D9ADAB129D.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.5C6688D9ADAB129D.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.5C8CF40663CCE754.quest_desc: ["The &6Diamond Hook&r increases the amount of hooks by 2, range of the hooks, and speed."]
	quest.5C9C7A5A88613109.quest_desc: [
		"Slimes can be found throughout the world. The Slime Vac can suck them up into inventory form using &6Shift + Right Click&r. "
		""
		"You can then fire them out using Right Click, if the Slime item is in your other hand. You can also suck up and shoot out items!"
		""
		"&oIf you look at the recipe in JEI using the Slime icon, you may find hints on where some types may be hiding.&r"
	]
	quest.5C9C7A5A88613109.title: "Slime Stealing"
	quest.5D6623B36EC39685.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.5D95CBE19118EAD4.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.5E89F151176083E6.quest_desc: ["The &6Extendo-Grip&r uses air to extend your reach for both placing, breaking, and attacking."]
	quest.5E89F151176083E6.quest_subtitle: "Extending Reach"
	quest.5FB57C45A25D41F0.quest_desc: [
		"Sunlit Valley is a more peaceful oriented modpack! This means:"
		""
		"- Inventory is kept on death (Though tool durability will be lost)"
		"- Mobs don't spawn above ground"
		"- Phantoms and Pillager patrols no longer spawn"
		"- Creepers are festive!"
		""
		"This doesn't mean there's no danger however. &6The underground, Nether, and Skull Cavern are as dangerous as ever&r...."
	]
	quest.5FB57C45A25D41F0.title: "More Peaceful Experience"
	quest.5FBE3685CF008A5A.quest_desc: [
		"Tiers of hoes above wood have abilities!"
		""
		"&6Shift+Right click&r to till in an area"
		""
		"&6Right click crops&r to harvest in an area"
		""
		"&6Left click grass/crops&r to destroy in an area (be careful with this one!)"
		""
		"The higher the tier, the larger the working area."
	]
	quest.5FBE3685CF008A5A.title: "Upgraded Hoes"
	quest.5FDA526D348C8A0F.quest_desc: [
		"The FTB Chunks map is disabled to prevent confusion from having two maps."
		""
		"If you're familiar with modded minecraft and prefer that map, click the check mark!"
		""
		"&cThis cannot be undone!&r"
	]
	quest.5FDA526D348C8A0F.title: "Prefer FTB Chunks?"
	quest.6080E8F9B0DDAE72.quest_subtitle: "Requires Botania"
	quest.6080E8F9B0DDAE72.title: "Manasteel Armor"
	quest.610689180666C83A.quest_subtitle: "Craftable Slime Heart"
	quest.610AB8B499859791.title: "Nether Fish Bundle"
	quest.611336F023B21ADF.quest_subtitle: "&6Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.6132A6DBE97F16BD.quest_desc: ["&6Fish Smokers&r are used to create smoked fish, which multiplies the value of a fish by &64&r in &62&r days. "]
	quest.6132A6DBE97F16BD.title: "Artisan Fish"
	quest.61501449BF31B773.quest_desc: [
		"By now your chests might be an overflowing mess."
		""
		"Luckily the &6Librarian villager&r sells a variety of items to help manage the mess."
		""
		"Most notable is the &6Controller&r, a block that can help manage entire storage systems. Items in its storage can be viewed using a &6Crafting Terminal&r placed next to it or connected with &6Cables&r."
		""
		""
	]
	quest.61501449BF31B773.title: "Farming Storage"
	quest.617AC2E80908BFD7.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter lists armor, tools, weapons, and other items that will help you on your journey to dominate the land."
		""
		"It also lays out the tool progression."
	]
	quest.617AC2E80908BFD7.title: "Equipment"
	quest.62129A6009E60E0F.quest_desc: [
		"Wondering what foods you can put on your menu?"
		""
		"In JEI/EMI's search bar you can search for &6#cozycafe:menu_items&r to find out! You can also search for just the specific types:"
		""
		"- &6#cozycafe:drink&r"
		"- &6#cozycafe:main&r"
		"- &6#cozycafe:dessert&r"
	]
	quest.62129A6009E60E0F.title: "Finding Menu Items"
	quest.62CB7BAB9BBB4030.quest_desc: [
		"During exploration you may have come across a &6Slime Heart&r. These are precious items that can be used to begin Slime Incubating!"
		""
		"To start, right click a &6Slime Incubator&r with the heart."
	]
	quest.62CB7BAB9BBB4030.title: "Slime Incubating"
	quest.632578AFE8A0D12D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Splendid Slimes&r are lovely creatures that produce a valuable byproduct when fed: &6Plorts&r!"
		""
		"They start out as wild, but once you feed them a food in their diet, they'll be tamed and won't despawn."
		""
		"They're simpler than farm animals, though you may find they cause a bit more chaos..."
	]
	quest.632578AFE8A0D12D.quest_subtitle: "Wrong Game?"
	quest.632578AFE8A0D12D.title: "Slime Ranching"
	quest.6327893DC34214E6.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.63F8C52D082BBCB3.quest_desc: [
		"The &dMagic Bulb&r is a strange device capable of harnessing the sun."
		""
		"It will require studying of all three ribbit artifacts to craft."
	]
	quest.63F8C52D082BBCB3.title: "Ribbit Sun Magic"
	quest.63FDC7BA6801CF64.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tackle Boxes&r are used to customize your rod using the slots on the right. They also retain their inventory when broken."
		""
		"&oOnly upgraded rods can have hooks attached&r"
	]
	quest.63FE67406861C9B5.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6412C4FB8294A6E2.quest_desc: [
		"&dPrismatic Shards&r are the ultimate form of power on Sunlit Valley."
		""
		"They craft into many of the most powerful items, and have various hidden uses. "
		""
		"They can be found more commonly the lower you go into the Skull Cavern, and can also be received from specific Skills."
	]
	quest.642F0375D7805A1B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Recycled Core&r is a smith's best friend, doubling the output of all &6Recycling Machine&r recipes. "
		""
		"It can be purchased from the &6Trader&r."
		""
		"&oRecipes similar to hook recycling do not double.&r"
	]
	quest.648FD0A599A54A0F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Corral Blocks&r keep your Slimes mostly safe, keeping them contained while allowing anything else to move in and out. "
		""
		"When given a redstone signal, they will prevent non-slime mobs from leaving as well."
	]
	quest.649860C19CAE0F17.quest_desc: ["Don't just stuff your farm with nameless livestock- naming a farm animal will make them like you a good bit more!"]
	quest.649860C19CAE0F17.title: "Pet Names"
	quest.64A93713A3B85B9A.quest_desc: [
		"Is your hotbar a mess? A &6Toolbelt&r can store your tools for quick access using a single hotkey (&6R&r by default)."
		""
		"By default it can only carry two slots, but multiple &6Belt Pouches&r can be sewn in for more slots."
	]
	quest.6541E0430F050B7D.title: "8,192 Bundle"
	quest.661A3A466ABF29BA.quest_desc: ["Only &66&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.661A3A466ABF29BA.title: "The Missing Bundle"
	quest.6635A53C7AF81CB3.quest_desc: ["The final tier of Sprinkler, the &6Iridium Sprinkler&r has the highest range out of any."]
	quest.664E4A3806C40A78.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Carpenter&r has two shops to browse through:"
		""
		"- &6Supplies&r, which has convenient building blocks"
		"- &6Invitations&r, which allow you to invite more villagers"
	]
	quest.66510F15A69EBAED.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hammers&r are powerful tools that will let you break multiple blocks at a time."
		""
		"They require cores to be crafted, and can be upgraded to increase range and metal tier."
		""
		"Unfortunately, &l&6they do not pass enchantments to the upgraded tool&r due to a bug that the modpack dev can't figure out. Sorry!"
	]
	quest.66510F15A69EBAED.title: "Mining Hammers"
	quest.6689D68F72E56A40.quest_desc: ["Buried in the depths of the &6The Nether&r "]
	quest.6689D68F72E56A40.title: "Nether Materia"
	quest.668AEE0B5CD49EE4.quest_desc: [
		"Each Slime breed has a favorite food. Feeding it to them will give them a big boost in happiness, while also causing them to produce &6double plorts&r!"
		""
		"Largo Slimes have multiple favorite foods, inherited from both breeds!"
	]
	quest.668AEE0B5CD49EE4.title: "Favorite Foods :pink_heart:"
	quest.66C1440EFF12DC66.quest_desc: [
		"Farming Slimes can be tricky! They all have different dreams and desires, and one wrong move will cause them to rip apart the fabric of your farm..."
		""
		"Luckily the &6Slime Inspector&r is here to help! Right clicking on a Slime with it will tell you if there's anything getting in the way of their happiness and your profits!"
	]
	quest.66D159252C70D5F2.quest_desc: [
		"Building a successful farm is not something you can do alone! Crafting the &6Carpenter Invitation&r is your next step!"
		""
		"The &6Carpenter&r can get you started, helping you build homes for new villagers and offering building supplies if you want to make them yourself."
		""
		"You can preview what all the different villager buildings given as quest rewards look like by talking to the Carpenter."
	]
	quest.66D159252C70D5F2.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Ace"
	quest.66D159252C70D5F2.title: "Starting Your Village"
	quest.66DEF5ED5F277804.quest_desc: ["Bone Meal cannot be used to grow crops, so you'll need to find more advanced and expensive options."]
	quest.66DEF5ED5F277804.title: "Weaker Bone Meal"
	quest.66E1AC55824DF1D9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Nether&r is the next area to exploit for its natural resources."
		""
		"Getting there will prove fairly trivial, but surviving is a trial for the unprepared..."
	]
	quest.66E1AC55824DF1D9.quest_subtitle: "Nether? I..."
	quest.6742B0BA3DD56AE8.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.67486880FE3E2CCD.quest_desc: [
		"This pack has a lot of animals that can make sounds that get old very quickly."
		""
		"To mute specific mobs/sounds, you can click on the volume icon in your inventory."
		""
		"If you dislike the ambient sounds in the pack, you can edit the file &6config/ambientsounds-client.json&r and set the volume to a lower value. You can also just remove the mod without losing the ability to connect to servers using the pack."
	]
	quest.67486880FE3E2CCD.quest_subtitle: "I can't stand the squirrels"
	quest.67486880FE3E2CCD.title: "Muting Sounds"
	quest.67622FAC6D509907.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.679F77E46148B5D1.quest_desc: [
		"By now you've probably become annoyed with storing the many items on your journey."
		""
		"A &6Backpack&r will come in handy, purchase one from the &6Market&r villager."
	]
	quest.679F77E46148B5D1.title: "Early Game Storage"
	quest.67F85F959DBBE0BD.title: "Collection: Cooking"
	quest.681EECD8B1D07F34.quest_desc: [
		"Skill paths split multiple times, and you might not like what you've picked!"
		""
		"Thankfully the &6Witch&r villager sells &6Crystals of Regret&r for each skill tree. They are one-time use, resetting your skill tree completely. "
		""
		"It refunds &65 skill points&r, so you don't have to start completely from 0."
	]
	quest.681EECD8B1D07F34.title: "Picked the Wrong Skills?"
	quest.68915F617033BDF9.quest_desc: [
		"Occasionally in the Skull Cavern you may come across a &6Trial Chamber&r."
		""
		"These dungeons are full of &6artifacts&r and &6relics&r, and can be found by using a key on a Trial Vault."
		""
		"Drinking an &6Ominous Bottle&r will give you better drops for fighting stronger mobs from the Trial Spawners."
	]
	quest.68915F617033BDF9.title: "Trial Chambers"
	quest.6933B95631B3A039.quest_desc: ["The &6Saw&r cuts logs into any type of wooden item. Useful for building or annoying crafts."]
	quest.693FFA0C3FD1A078.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sharestones&r are sold by the &6Witch&r and can be used to teleport to any of the same color."
		""
		"Collecting all 4 will let you craft them into a &6Waystone&r which has the same functionality, but lets you teleport to them using scrolls and Warp Stones."
	]
	quest.693FFA0C3FD1A078.title: "Waystones \\& Sharestones"
	quest.6971F0B3FC26D411.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Oil Maker&r is an Artisan Machine for turning rough products into valuable artisanal oil."
		""
		"Its best use is for making &6Truffle Oil&r"
	]
	quest.69C3121C90AABBF4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Controller&r can't actually store any items on its own. "
		""
		"Existing chests or other inventories such as Drawers can be added to the network using an &6External Storage&r."
		""
		"If you prefer digitally storing items for easy transportation, &64k Storage Blocks&r can be placed to allow for up to &64,000&r items on its own."
	]
	quest.69C3121C90AABBF4.title: "Adding Storage Space"
	quest.6A580C44B2AEF52F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Harvesters&r are the ultimate form of crop collecting, allowing you to automate your farm completely."
		""
		"Once crafted, they can be duplicated using a cheaper recipe."
	]
	quest.6A5A513E8C0455AF.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.6A931F456D6FEA3E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Water Wheels&r are the cheapest form of power crafted from simple materials."
		""
		"They will move once they hit flowing water, and can be connected to Belts and machines using &6Shafts&r."
	]
	quest.6A931F456D6FEA3E.title: "First Power"
	quest.6A94BB4CB99D814E.quest_desc: [
		"The first layer of the Skull Cavern is relatively safe. It contains a variety of overworld ores, and it doesn't present much danger to you."
		""
		"&oYou should aim to get through this area as fast as possible...&r"
	]
	quest.6A94BB4CB99D814E.title: "Layer I - The Cavern Shallows"
	quest.6ADD884F3FFE5D42.quest_desc: [
		"Your journey into farming starts with the &6Market&r, which sells a variety of basic seeds."
		""
		"Some crops only grow in certain seasons, which is designated in the crops's tooltip. "
		""
		"Seasons last &630 minecraft days&r, and hot or cold biomes will be always be Summer and Winter respectively."
		""
		"Equipping the Calendar will show the current sub-season in the top left of your screen."
	]
	quest.6ADD884F3FFE5D42.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Leon"
	quest.6ADD884F3FFE5D42.title: "Starting Farming"
	quest.6C1236C00210E5A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hammer&r can be used to crush stones into other forms, i.e Stone -> Cobblestone -> Gravel."
		""
		""
		"The &6Chisel&r turns blocks into their chiseled variants if they exist."
	]
	quest.6C1236C00210E5A7.title: "Chiseling and Cracking"
	quest.6C342B7B66C29823.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sharestones&r can teleport you to any of the same color. All 4 are needed to attain perfection."
		""
		"&oYou don't have to read the other Sharestone quests.&r"
	]
	quest.6C656EEBAD2B5DAF.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.6C656EEBAD2B5DAF.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.6C729A76F44E32D0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scribe&r can be used to break glass fast and always drop it. It can also be used to create grooves in ice."
		""
		"Very useful for moving your greenhouse."
	]
	quest.6C7A3AB4B9DEA9A7.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.6C7C42BC9E072DE1.title: "Complete the Boiler Room"
	quest.6C95E6AEEC55CFA5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bismuth Ingots&r can be made into a special glass that forms &6Classic Pipes&r."
		""
		"When given a redstone signal, &6Copper Pipes&r can extract items from inventories and insert them into &6Item Pipes&r that route them in different directions."
		""
		"Different types of pipes can be used to create handy systems for item transport on your farm."
	]
	quest.6C95E6AEEC55CFA5.title: "Item Transport"
	quest.6D534E699BF820CE.quest_desc: [
		"Hand feeding animals can be a challenge with the amount of everyday farming chores. "
		""
		"A &6Feeding Trough&r does this for you to any animals in range, provided it has Animal Feed."
	]
	quest.6D5F31A96631A62D.title: "Complete the Pantry"
	quest.6DAD35E264D3E056.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Wand of Symmetry&r places a mirror in the world that mirrors block placement."
		""
		"Shift + Right click lets you switch the pattern of placement."
	]
	quest.6DAD35E264D3E056.title: "Placing Symmetrically"
	quest.6E4CC63B8CF1EDAF.title: "Terrasteel Armor"
	quest.6E7B80C8D3FD952D.quest_desc: ["&6Lightspeed Rails&r have an extremely high max speed, but can't slope or turn."]
	quest.6EA5618181628D34.quest_desc: [
		"This pack has a configuration! Things like multiplayer sharestones or hospital fees can be turned on or off."
		""
		"In the modpack folder, go to the folder &6kubejs&r and then &6startup_scripts&r."
		""
		"Find the file &6_config.js&r, and open it up with Notepad. Update the values save the file, and restart the game."
		""
		"If you're on a server, the server admin may need to change these values as well."
	]
	quest.6EA5618181628D34.quest_subtitle: "Want to change something? Do it!"
	quest.6EA5618181628D34.title: "Configuring the Pack"
	quest.6EB1FF96F5B7DC7C.quest_subtitle: "Overworld Structures"
	quest.6EBAA004C1A50E98.quest_desc: ["Completeting the Abandoned Farm gives you a &3Petal Apothecary&r. This is your entry point into Botania, a magical automation mod that will help with certain tasks around the farm."]
	quest.6EBAA004C1A50E98.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Petal Apothecary (Botania)"
	quest.6EBAA004C1A50E98.title: "Abandoned Farm Completed!"
	quest.6EEBD017839FF628.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, raising farm animals requires care, money, and attention. "
		""
		"A &6Shepherd&r villager will be needed for basic supplies."
	]
	quest.6EEBD017839FF628.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Maria"
	quest.6EEBD017839FF628.title: "Raising Farm Animals"
	quest.6F3F87DBBBE86A28.title: "Winter Bundle"
	quest.6F3FC6227213B886.quest_desc: [
		"Crops have 3 different tiers of Quality: &7Iron&r, &6Gold&r, and &dIridium&r."
		""
		"The value of the crop increases based on the tier of quality, and is reflected in the tooltip!"
	]
	quest.6F3FC6227213B886.title: "Crop Quality"
	quest.6F565AC5DF217E39.quest_subtitle: "Overworld Structures, Skull Cavern"
	quest.6F8709C925DE7237.quest_desc: [
		"As you wander around the world you might notice &6Butterflies&r and &6Moths&r flying around! "
		""
		"With a &6Catching Net&r, you can pick them up and collect each of the different kinds."
		""
		"While they will never be the most profitable part of your farm, building a sanctuary for these creatures will provide you with unique benefits."
	]
	quest.6F8709C925DE7237.quest_subtitle: "Butterflies and Moths"
	quest.6F8709C925DE7237.title: "Catching Longwings"
	quest.6FDA9C1E5D681CDA.quest_desc: ["&eElectrum Armor&r increases the speed of the user by a significant amount, making them ideal for long range travel. "]
	quest.6FDA9C1E5D681CDA.quest_subtitle: "Requires Create or Botania"
	quest.6FDA9C1E5D681CDA.title: "Electrum Armor"
	quest.6FE9F992ACD90629.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fish Ponds&r cultivate fish over time once a single fish is placed in. Roe and other items can be harvested from them, and more items are unlocked at certain fish populations. "
		""
		"Sometimes the fish will request items in order to grow their populaton."
		""
		"You'll need a 3x4 of water (or lava for nether fish) behind the pond according to this professional diagram:"
		""
		"&3⬜⬜⬜"
		"&3⬜⬜⬜"
		"&3⬜⬜⬜ <- Water/Lava"
		"&3⬜⬜⬜"
		"  &6⬜   <- Fish Pond block"
		""
		"{image:society:textures/gui/fish_pond_example.png width:150 height:150 align:center}"
		""
	]
	quest.6FE9F992ACD90629.title: "Farming Fish"
	quest.702A9E699FC422CC.quest_desc: ["&6Iron Hooks&r have two hooks, allowing you to float in midair."]
	quest.7037A26BF990653E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Trader&r is willing to move into your town after noticing your work in the Skull Cavern!"
		""
		"Unlike most other shops, money has no value here. You'll need to trade specific items to afford the trader's wares..."
	]
	quest.7037A26BF990653E.quest_subtitle: "Welcoming Carlos"
	quest.7037A26BF990653E.title: "Bartering?"
	quest.70E664D2389F628D.quest_subtitle: "Not counted in Completionist Banner"
	quest.711AC0F5208316D5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mincer&r is a cooking implement for finely grounding certain items. "
		""
		"It is a necessary tool for when chopping can't quite get the job done."
	]
	quest.71C32483EE2418CA.quest_desc: [
		"Teleportation is rare and expensive in this pack, encouraging you to build out your infrastructure at first."
		""
		"If you cannot live without it, take a look at the \"Paving The Road\" quest first."
	]
	quest.71C32483EE2418CA.title: "Teleportation Options"
	quest.723A5C8DB06D8C36.quest_desc: [
		"It might be the time to open up your first Cafe!"
		""
		"The &6Cafe Manager&r will allow you to create a place where customers come to eat at. The menu is fully customizable, allowing you to serve whatever your farm specializes in."
		""
		"Items sold in your cafe are worth &650%% more&r! Fast service will also get you up to&6 100%% more&r in tips. Your skills will also be used, making this worth the time investment. "
	]
	quest.723A5C8DB06D8C36.title: "Opening a Cozy Cafe"
	quest.7282287A6621FF82.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Blaze Burner&r can be filled by right clicking a Blaze or Blaze Spawner with the empty version of it."
		""
		"It can be placed below a Basin and Mixer and given fuel to craft alloys."
	]
	quest.7282287A6621FF82.title: "Metal Alloying"
	quest.729467D224F25987.quest_desc: [
		"There's no reason to kill your farm animals you love and care for!"
		""
		"&6Magic Shears&r will allow you to harvest their drops using otherworldy magic on right click."
		""
		"Animals will only let you do this if they have high enough affection, and it can only be done once per day."
	]
	quest.729467D224F25987.title: "Cruelty Free Meat"
	quest.72CCDB6B078E8908.quest_desc: ["&6Ancient Fruits&r take an excrutiatingly long time to grow. It's best to focus on getting more seeds with the first few harvests before jumping into profits."]
	quest.73A85902CE35A43A.quest_desc: [
		"There are 6 main tiers of &6Coins&r, and they can be crafted up or down from the previous tier."
		""
		"These are their values:"
		""
		"- Copper (&61&r)"
		"- Zinc (&68&r)"
		"- Iron (&616&r)"
		"- Brass (&664&r)"
		"- Gold (&6512&r)"
		"- Iridium (&64096&r)"
	]
	quest.73A85902CE35A43A.title: "All About Coins"
	quest.73E15D00539BF7CD.quest_desc: [
		"There are occasions where you may need a large quantity of one specific fish. The &6Bait Maker&r turns one of any type of fish into targeted bait!"
		""
		"This bait can be placed inside of a &6Crab Trap&r,"
		""
		"&oNether Fish can be caught in a Crab Trap placed in water... Strange.&r"
	]
	quest.7466DCDD6C3CDDE8.quest_desc: ["Only &65&r required for bundle completion."]
	quest.7466DCDD6C3CDDE8.title: "Brewing Bundle"
	quest.747B28CA5F55AFA7.quest_desc: [
		"Sllimes can be turned into a &6Largo&r by feeding a &6Plort&r of a different breed to it!"
		""
		"Largos inherit all the qualities of both slimes, dropping one plort of each kind."
		""
		"But be careful, feeding a Largo a third type of plort will turn it into a &6Tarr&r- an evil creature that gobbles up nearby slimes..."
	]
	quest.747B28CA5F55AFA7.title: "Largoit!"
	quest.74CB97A6B1ADC2B8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Belts&r can be attached to shafts to move items around when powered. &6Funnels&r can be attached to inventories to allow belts to feed into them."
		""
		"This is the primary method of moving items around in Create."
	]
	quest.74CB97A6B1ADC2B8.title: "Moving Items Around"
	quest.75181B22DAF5E9A6.quest_desc: [
		"Milk can be pressed into cheese using an &6Artisan Cheese Press&r."
		""
		"&oYou'll want to take a look at the farming quest line for information on how to get the ingredients for one.&r"
	]
	quest.751852642BED95D0.quest_desc: ["Fruit tree sapling a possible reward from a &5Prize Machine&r."]
	quest.751852642BED95D0.quest_subtitle: "&5Prize Machine"
	quest.75472A79424BCD40.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hypertubes&r are a transportation method that uses rotational power to zoop you around your base."
		""
		"The &6Entrance Block&r requires rotational power, and two of them can be linked using &6Hypertube Blocks&r using the same rules as train tracks."
	]
	quest.75472A79424BCD40.title: "Tubular Transport"
	quest.7591439B35772AB2.quest_desc: [
		"The reward for completing the Crafts Room is the magnificant &6Magic Mirror&r!"
		""
		"This item takes you to your bed/spawn when used, provided its in range of the mirror."
		""
		"&6Relic Experience&r can be used to upgrade the range."
	]
	quest.7591439B35772AB2.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Magic Mirror"
	quest.7591439B35772AB2.title: "Crafts Room Completed!"
	quest.761F68396065119B.quest_desc: ["Crab Traps will provide certain fish, junk, or treasure over time. They must be surrounded by a 3x3 of water, and be provided with &6Crab Trap Bait&r."]
	quest.76672EF7299492DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sparkpods&r are rough otherworldly fruits that can be sourced from the &6Market&r. "
		""
		"They are filled with energy and can be mashed into &6Sparkstone&r using a variety of methods."
		""
		"Unlike most crops, they are unable to be cultivated using a &6Seed Maker&r..."
	]
	quest.766BAE4A5160FD13.quest_desc: [
		"&6Refined Storage&r systems are convenient, but the limited range can be limiting in some scenarios. "
		""
		"The &6Dimension Card&r will allow you to access your storage from anywhere when placed in a &6Wireless Transmitter&r."
		""
		"You'll need to make sure your storage system is chunk loaded for this to work. See the Welcome chapter for info on &6Claiming Chunks&r if you don't know how!"
	]
	quest.769AC695FD3F8DC9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sharestones&r can teleport you to any of the same color. All 4 are needed to attain perfection."
		""
		"&oYou don't have to read the other Sharestone quests.&r"
	]
	quest.76A35BBCA4E0CDD9.title: "River Fish Bundle"
	quest.76A60EE6F3E0FF72.quest_desc: [
		"Unlocking &6Adventuring Mastery&r allows you to take your beloved pets on grand adventures without the fear of losing them! It also allows more options with enchanting past the skill tree enchantments."
		""
		"Once unlocked, certain associated items can be bought from the &6Guild&r and &6Witch&r."
	]
	quest.771697176D1B54CD.title: "Collection: Relics"
	quest.7718055315817CB1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lead&r and &6Silver&r ingots can be automated using various machines. "
		""
		"&6Silver&r can be produced using &6Alchemical Varnish&r, a renewably farmable fluid."
		""
		"&6Lead&r can be multiplied using &6Crushed Obsidian&r as an additive."
	]
	quest.7718055315817CB1.quest_subtitle: "Skip out on the mining!"
	quest.77690255DF58F118.quest_desc: [
		"Bobbers can be attached to any kind of fishing rod by dragging it over and right clicking on it."
		""
		"They have various effects on the fishing minigame, such as revealing the fish on the line or increasing the bobber size even more!"
	]
	quest.77690255DF58F118.title: "Minigame modifications"
	quest.77780C73C016EE60.title: "Complete the Fish Tank"
	quest.77E2AE3656E32182.quest_desc: [
		"Hoarding your coins in random chests isn't ideal. The &6Bank Terminal&r is an ATM, allowing you to store your coins safely. You can access your money from any other Bank Terminal, like an Ender Chest."
		""
		"It can be purchased from the &6Banker&r villager."
	]
	quest.77E2AE3656E32182.title: "Storing Money"
	quest.785F3754068D5C2D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Needle Bobber&r and &6Net Bobbers&r are two sides of the same coin, making the fishing minigame much more difficult for a huge boost in rewards."
		""
		"They'll only be useful to rod champion (or a person that's just upgraded their rod a ton)."
	]
	quest.785F3754068D5C2D.title: "Masterful Bobbers"
	quest.79C92AEDE15E7E6D.quest_desc: [
		"Crops can be processed in a &6Fermenting Jar&r to increase their value and nutrition."
		""
		"There also have a few utility recipes for farms, such as Froglights and Slime Blocks."
	]
	quest.7A159242A6B053C8.quest_desc: ["Cook all dishes from &6Let's Do: Bakery&r."]
	quest.7A159242A6B053C8.title: "Bakery Blaster"
	quest.7A5974D470C5AA9C.quest_desc: ["&6Gold&r armors have increased protection and durability to &6Iron&r, unlike what you might expect in vanilla Minecraft."]
	quest.7A5974D470C5AA9C.title: "Gold Armor"
	quest.7A7B131D229E5279.quest_desc: [
		"Spice of Life: Onion Edition has been added to incentivize eating different foods."
		""
		"Reaching certain thresholds of food diversity will give you benefits listed in the book. Most notably: extra health!"
	]
	quest.7A7B131D229E5279.title: "The Spice of Life"
	quest.7AA369DD63BC7331.quest_subtitle: "Overworld Structures, Nether"
	quest.7ADD57C8AF4092B2.quest_desc: [
		"Butterflies and Moths can be lured to your base using different types of brews!"
		""
		"You can right click on a &6Butterfly Drip-Lure&r to fill it. Different types of brews will attract different kinds."
	]
	quest.7ADD57C8AF4092B2.title: "Tasty Luring"
	quest.7B08E22C0E8DE900.quest_subtitle: "&6Copper or Reinforced Brewingstation"
	quest.7B26713E5E4E25CB.quest_desc: [
		"As you dive deeper into the Skull Cavern, you might encounter something called &dSparkstone&r."
		""
		"It is a gem filled with intense energy that can be used to power advanced farming equipment for automation."
	]
	quest.7B26713E5E4E25CB.title: "The Automation Era"
	quest.7B2AB58CA9C1C19B.quest_desc: ["The &6Barkeeper&r sells food and various multiplayer-oriented items, such as &6Cameras&r and &6Easels&r."]
	quest.7B2AB58CA9C1C19B.title: "Barkeeper"
	quest.7B2EB2B56F155E49.quest_desc: ["&6Oak Resin&r is tapped from oak logs, and is used as a sealant for many fluid-related items."]
	quest.7BA3A7D6D37CFA69.title: "Mineral Collection Complete!"
	quest.7BCC4E221CF97D0B.quest_desc: ["&6Frames&r are placeholder blocks for builds that can be quickly replaced by right clicking with a block. "]
	quest.7BCC4E221CF97D0B.title: "Framing out a Building"
	quest.7BFB656868B2395C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Holograph Rails&r project holographic rails outwards. "
		""
		"They can be angled upwards by applying a redstone signal. "
		""
		"There are wooden and maglev variants, with a shorter and longer max length respectively."
	]
	quest.7BFB656868B2395C.title: "Holograph Rails"
	quest.7C30FC21953CF7D3.quest_desc: [
		"Main dishes in your &6cafe&r will need to be plated before serving!"
		""
		"A &6Plating Station&r is used to plate these items."
		""
		"Note that dishes that already come with a bowl will not need to be plated, if you prefer not washing dishes!"
	]
	quest.7C30FC21953CF7D3.title: "Plating Up"
	quest.7CBAF0748446A0C2.quest_desc: [
		"Collecting crops of every season and animal products completes the Pantry. This rewards you with a building containing &648 Greenhouse Glass&r. This valuable material allows crops of any season to grow when the glass is at most 16 blocks above the crop."
		""
		"You can also choose to just receive the glass itself, if you'd like to build your own greenhouse."
	]
	quest.7CBAF0748446A0C2.quest_subtitle: "Reward: Greenhouse Starter"
	quest.7CBAF0748446A0C2.title: "Pantry Completed!"
	quest.7CE6C320CC9F9B87.title: "2,048 Bundle"
	quest.7D1394F6356086D0.quest_desc: [
		"Some biomes such as &6Savannas&r and &6Jungles&r will always be treated as &6Summer&r for crop growth only. They will be marked as \"Wet Season\" and \"Dry Season\"."
		""
		"This can be used to create a secondary farm that has no need to worry about seasons!"
		""
		"The same applies to frozen biomes for &6Winter&r."
	]
	quest.7D1394F6356086D0.title: "Eternal Summer"
	quest.7D155FD0EFEEB5AC.title: "Spring Crops Bundle"
	quest.7D25F7C2281DBCD0.quest_desc: [
		"Expensive and slow, the &6Crystalarium&r will duplicate any gem or mineral placed inside. The amount of days to complete will depend on the inserted item."
		""
		"They should be your first goal if you dislike mining for crafting minerals."
	]
	quest.7D25F7C2281DBCD0.title: "Growing Crystals"
	quest.7D61ED4C5AB846F5.quest_subtitle: "Ancient Cities"
	quest.7E69F542D4EDE72B.title: "Crop Collection Complete!"
	quest.7E94B1934D0257E8.quest_desc: ["Tired of hearing your Villagers? Click the \"mute\" icon in your inventory to open up the &6Extreme Sound Muffler&r GUI, allowing you to mute specific sounds!"]
	quest.7E94B1934D0257E8.title: "Muting Sounds"
	quest.7ED74D28362C25CE.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit tree sapling can be purchased from the &6Market&r after your first year."
		""
		"You'll need to find a &dPrismatic Shard&r deep in the Skull Cavern to craft their workstation."
	]
	quest.7ED74D28362C25CE.quest_subtitle: "&6Market after first year"
	quest.7EE92D71D7478FA4.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Crowbar&r can get you out of a ditch by completely breaking apart your car, but is very much a last resort option. "
		""
		"The &6Car Key&r solves this issue by letting you \"park\" an Automobility vehicle inside of it."
	]
	quest.7EE92D71D7478FA4.title: "Long Term Parking"
	quest.7FFED918C5367350.quest_desc: [
		"You found a &6Geode&r! Place it in your offhand, and right click with a &6Geode Buster&r to open it."
		""
		"If you're lucky you might get a valuable gem."
		""
		"If not, there's more where that came from! Geode Busters can be bought from the &6Blacksmith&r villager."
	]
	quest.7FFED918C5367350.title: "Eggs of the King"
